{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm","id":1288173,"title":"\u200bAre Lunar\u2019s too mono-focused on the Realm?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-14T22:26:00-08:00","id":1288173,"title":"\u200bAre Lunar\u2019s too mono-focused on the Realm?","content":"First off I want to say I actually am enjoying the lunar chapters so far. However, I am also finding their focus a bit too narrow.<br /> <br /> Now, as a DB fan I like the realm. Also as a fan I admit it would be fun to rip the Realm apart for it many and various sins then dance among the embers. The Silver pack I feel should represent a martial force as presented because of the history of creation and the dominance of the Realm through a very large proportion of the world. That said I also feel there should have been mentioned that there are other groups of Lunars that are focused on different things based on their location. Creation is vast and I could see in distant areas where the shogunate has faded from memory and that the blessed island would seem like some distant magic land if the people knew it existed at all. Heck, from what I have read the Realm is just now exploring the west. Given the vast area of creation it would have been nice to see a group or two separate from the Silver Pack or Shahan-ya with no focus on war with the realm at all. If only because the Realm is so far away that they might not even know that it exists or it might have almost no consequence to them compared to say fair-folk raiders or local spirit politics for just two of many examples.<br /> <br /> I guess what I am saying is why should the medicine man of a far north eastern tribe care about some empire he only vaguely knows of compared to fighting cruel winter gods, heartless fair-folk with skin of ice, and strange beasts born under a strange sign in the sky? Perhaps I am being overly finicky but I think it would have been interesting to explore those groups detached from struggle against the realm, even if only a small paragraph or one to two examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T22:59:09-08:00","id":1288179,"title":"","content":"But there have been a number of example Lunars in the chapter, even as members of the Silver Pact, whose concern with the Realm is minimal at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T23:03:20-08:00","id":1288181,"title":"","content":"Well right now the chapter we've got has been more focused on the Silver Pact itself, which was pretty much founded on the premise of destroying the organizations that spring up to take the ruler of the world spot the Solar Deliberative used to have if its not the Lunars in charge. Consequently, we've also been focusing more on the larger players of it and their stances which invariably go to towards the Realm as the most easy point of reference. Remember a Shahan-ya is a title in the Silver Pact, so Leviathan wasn't going to be a Shahan-ya to any Lunars he trained if it was before the Realm's excursions made him decide to stop moping at Luthe. The Realm is also always going to be at least a thing one pays attention to seeing how as a Lunar one is automatically anathema and thus drawing any attention from the Realm will probably make them want to kill you.<br /> <br /> As for the sole focus well we do have some mention already of Lunars who are more focused on other things than the Realm. Ajna Silverclaws is a noted to not be that interested in the Realm being more interested in Thorns. <br /> <br /> So really I'd put it more down to the fact that the Silver Pact is focused on the Realm and The Realm being the world's only superpower makes it the big problem that most will deal with. That said also remember that the Silver Pact has a policy that if you don't want to join them off the bat then you're free to go and do your own thing. The Pact is generally assuming that given a couple years or decades you'll probably have dealt with whatever &quot;lesser problems&quot; you're currently focused or are more willing to get involved with the big picture problem of the Shogunate, its successor The Realm, and preventing having to deal with a 3rd generation successor to that group.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T23:07:44-08:00","id":1288182,"title":"","content":"Its really hard for a lunar to completely and totally ignore the Realm unless they plan on spending all their time in the ass end of the edges of Creation where even they have difficulty getting a Wyld Hunt going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T23:16:04-08:00","id":1288184,"title":"","content":"I mean they are also pretty focused on mounting the heads of the five score fellowship on pikes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T23:17:39-08:00","id":1288185,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, yeah it might be a bit too focused in the chapters we\u2019ve seen so far, but the Silver Pact is, among other things, a mosaic of resistance cells and the Realm is the Empire that they\u2019re resisting. There are other more local concerns but the Realm is the unifying one. My guess is we\u2019ll see a broader focus in other areas of the book, and in Many Faced Strangers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T23:24:30-08:00","id":1288186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288184#post1288184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean they are also pretty focused on mounting the heads of the five score fellowship on pikes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stuff we have seen makes it seem like the ones sufficiently in the know to realize that not all Sidereals are part of the bronze faction are generally willing to give the ones that aren't a shot (unless they are a first age elder that helped with the usurpation despite breaking away from the bronze faction later like Rakan Thulio). For example, Raksi apparently worked with a gold faction Sidereal to banish some demon that was threatening Creation and slaughter their cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T23:30:07-08:00","id":1288187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288186#post1288186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The stuff we have seen makes it seem like the ones sufficiently in the know to realize that not all Sidereals are part of the bronze faction are generally willing to give the ones that aren't a shot (unless they are a first age elder that helped with the usurpation despite breaking away from the bronze faction later like Rakan Thulio). For example, Raksi apparently worked with a gold faction Sidereal to banish some demon that was threatening Creation and slaughter their cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that seems to be mostly the G1 Lunars (like Raksi). 99% ish of Lunars are probably on board with plan pike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T23:31:26-08:00","id":1288188,"title":"","content":"Give me a minute, I'll compile every example whose interest in fighting the Realm is little to non-existent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T23:56:20-08:00","id":1288192,"title":"","content":"That would be useful actually Isator.<br /> Snakesandsuns is not alone; I was discussing Fangs at the Gate with one of my friends yesterday, who doesn't really like it so far, and his biggest complaint is that Lunars seem to be all about fighting the Realm, which is too restrictive. <br /> Like Snakesandsuns, he questioned why a shaman in a marsh far from the Realm should Exalt and suddenly it's all about fighting the Realm.<br /> (Which segued into an interesting discussion about how, by removing the Thousand Dooms, the Realm is massively emphasised as the villains, but that's a separate point.)<br /> <br /> In fact, the Realm has rarely been the primary antagonists of our games. In my game, which started in the Hundred Kingdoms, it was Abyssals, and later a rival group of Celestials. In my friend's game there's been a whole variety, but we've been in a country very far South for ages, where the Realm's not an issue.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't quite agree; of course the Silver Pact chapter is all about fighting the Realm, but that doesn't mean that the Domains chapter will be. I can see where he's coming from though.<br /> <br /> (I was thinking about how, in a game a different friend runs, I believe they have been fighting Lookshy; the Silver Pact chapter actually says they oppose all Dragonblood groups who continue the legacy of the Shogunate. Yet I don't think that fighting Lookshy or Prasad is much mentioned.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T02:29:36-08:00","id":1288213,"title":"","content":"I'm not terribly concerned.<br /> The Silver Pact's general direction doesn\u2019t need to matter to any games any more than what the Lunars who aren\u2019t part of the PCs pack think is more important and it's a slightly more palatable answer than &quot;I'd love to help you with the Mask of Winters sport, but I'm three generations into turning a caste system into a meritocracy and if I don't micromanage I come back and the whole place is on fire, you know how it is?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T08:28:16-08:00","id":1288268,"title":"","content":"'Fighting the Realm' is a <i>bit</i> overstated. The Lunars' overall goal can be stated simply, but it's not that statement. It's 'Avenge the Usurpation'. Just like the 'simple' Sidereal 'mission statement' is 'protect the Fate of Creation'. Solars and DBs can't be summed up quite <i>that</i> simply, but it's still in that vein.<br /> <br /> So while the Lunar focus on the Realm can be seen, it's a symptom, not a goal. They're equally 'focused' on destroying the Bronze Faction, Lookshy, and every other remnant that proclaims to derive authority from the Usurpation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:22:36-08:00","id":1288289,"title":"","content":"Eh........<br /> <br /> For Elders, sure. For most young Lunars, the Usurpation is ancient history. Their goals are going to be about whoever's threatening them and those they love now. In a lot of cases, that's the Realm (and in others... it's not).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T09:50:54-08:00","id":1288301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288289#post1288289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh........<br /> <br /> For Elders, sure. For most young Lunars, the Usurpation is ancient history. Their goals are going to be about whoever's threatening them and those they love now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth considering that who they love is, in many cases, going to extend to other Lunars, especially under the circumstances in which they first meet.<br /> <br /> Even if those circumstances have nothing to do with saving them from the Wyld Hunt. Other Lunars give you your Caste, and that's surely a profound, powerful experience. Many Lunars are extremely compelling, impressive figures in their own right; some, evidently, more than they really like.<br /> <br /> And then there are the Lunars who are not threatened personally, but can be swayed by the arguments of those that are already invested, whether it's appealing to principle or material benefits or what relationships have developed.<br /> <br /> How good at propaganda do you think the Silver Pact are? As good as ISIS? I know that my standards for believable ideological shifts changed when I read about some of the people that joined ISIS.<br /> <br /> I think it's going to happen disproportionately, because the Silver Pact is dedicated to it. Not just out of a desire for more recruits for their crusade, but because they constitute a form of continuity from a standard of Lunar relations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a lot of cases, that's the Realm (and in others... it's not).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and when it's not, there's no controversy about them being barely associated or truly independent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:03:35-08:00","id":1288331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288182#post1288182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its really hard for a lunar to completely and totally ignore the Realm unless they plan on spending all their time in the ass end of the edges of Creation where even they have difficulty getting a Wyld Hunt going.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the same time there are a lot of really cool game ideas that can occur on the ass-edges of Creation where an entire game can go by without the Realm ever being even a minor antagonist player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:36:40-08:00","id":1288340,"title":"","content":"There's nothing wrong with having more important priorities than the Realm -- but the one thing <i>all</i> Lunars have in common is that the Realm is their enemy.<br /> <br /> You have to be pretty far from the Blessed Isle before you can afford to ignore the Realm, and the bigger your ambitions get, the more certain it is that someone Realm-affiliated will take notice of the filthy Anathema doing [insert ambitious activity here] and move to intercept. And if you start trading favors with other Lunars, you're going to end up acting directly against the Realm sooner or later. Even if you don't give a damn about the Realm, helping others fight them might end up being the fastest way to secure allies for your own interests.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I entirely like the statement that the Silver Pact is &quot;first and foremost&quot; a weapon against Dragon-Blooded hegemony, but it probably is a natural result of the fact that every Lunar over a certain age almost certainly carries a grudge against the Realm for <i>something</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:55:55-08:00","id":1288347,"title":"","content":"I don't get it. The core book describing in explicit detail that there are Lunars, a decent number of them, that weren't affiliated with the Pact was one of the first things that stood out to me, and it seems to be widely overlooked elsewhere.<br /> <br /> The Lunars book contains frequent references to them, more than I'd have called for had it been my decision (I would have been wrong), and it's alternately not enough or just kind of missed?<br /> <br /> Wh- what more do people want? In terms of internal logic and gameplay and setting design, there's reasonable purpose behind the Silver Pact being prominent. What else can be done with the margins besides pointing out they exist, describing a bit of how they relate from a distance to the Pact, and dotting examples of people like that across the book?<br /> <br /> Especially considering how it effectively makes the Silver Pact feel very loose. You can technically be a member, but nobody is going to be intermittently showing up at your door asking for your membership due of one hundred Dynast scalps. You're not barred from attending councils. Friends and allies might ask for payment in something hostile to the Realm in exchange for their aid, but is that ultimately very different from propiating some god by going off to fight a dangerous cave monster?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T12:45:10-08:00","id":1288365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288331#post1288331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the same time there are a lot of really cool game ideas that can occur on the ass-edges of Creation where an entire game can go by without the Realm ever being even a minor antagonist player.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T12:47:17-08:00","id":1288367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288347#post1288347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get it. The core book describing in explicit detail that there are Lunars, a decent number of them, that weren't affiliated with the Pact was one of the first things that stood out to me, and it seems to be widely overlooked elsewhere.<br /> <br /> The Lunars book contains frequent references to them, more than I'd have called for had it been my decision (I would have been wrong), and it's alternately not enough or just kind of missed?<br /> <br /> Wh- what more do people want? In terms of internal logic and gameplay and setting design, there's reasonable purpose behind the Silver Pact being prominent. What else can be done with the margins besides pointing out they exist, describing a bit of how they relate from a distance to the Pact, and dotting examples of people like that across the book?<br /> <br /> Especially considering how it effectively makes the Silver Pact feel very loose. You can technically be a member, but nobody is going to be intermittently showing up at your door asking for your membership due of one hundred Dynast scalps. You're not barred from attending councils. Friends and allies might ask for payment in something hostile to the Realm in exchange for their aid, but is that ultimately very different from propiating some god by going off to fight a dangerous cave monster?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't blame them for now, after all the silver pact is the focus in whats been released so far, they are reading the part of WFHW about the Scarlet Dynasty and wondering why it isn't talking more about Lookshy or Outcastes. I'm sure later parts of the book will give some more focus on lunars that aren't part of it instead of just saying 'yeah they are totally there'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T13:25:00-08:00","id":1288380,"title":"","content":"Leaving aside the &quot;If you don't care about the Realm, the Realm cares about you&quot; side of it, and past life grudges, and mortal life, leaving aside all that, if that doesn't touch you at all, the Silver Pact and members thereof being able to effective trade you aid and support for what you do care about in exchange for joining in with their struggle will probably tend to entangle you.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are Lunars who stay totally outside those concerns, but I don't think we have to consider that all Lunars who are involved do get involved because of a personal grudge from their mortal or early Exalt lives or to mitigate the threat the Realm is actively presenting to them. Many will get persuaded in, and/or sucked in by trading support to other Lunars that doesn't seem like that big a deal at the time, etc. Social structures built around resistance and opposition can become *really* absorbing to anyone's individual identity and goals, even if you only let them in for reasons that seem totally pragmatic and non-burdensome at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T13:47:14-08:00","id":1288385,"title":"","content":"Might I suggest a slightly different interpretation? <br /> <br /> The Silver Pact as a whole clearly has the Realm high on its list of concerns, in fact, the need to deal with them is probably one of the few things that have universal support among its members. However, the Silver Pact is not monolithic either - it has a number of shahan-yas aren't all that concerned with the Realm. The Pact is to the Lunars what the Realm is to the Dragonblooded, a central organization that many (though not all) exist in that has set interests that may or may not comport with any number of its component factions. I will say that I think part this issue is that a lot of the writing tends to be framed around their reaction to the Realm, as in a Shahan-ya will be mentioned as unconcerned with the Realm as opposed to concerned about the Raksha.<br /> <br /> I would hope that further material will talk more about their concerns with the Raksha especially since we don't know a ton about them in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T16:47:21-08:00","id":1288435,"title":"","content":"I'm actually pleased with how the book focuses on politics and motives that have nothing to do with the Realm.<br /> <br /> Raks, Ma-ha-Suchi and Shadow Fang Vanguard are more focused on their rivalry and their political visions than they are on war with the realm. Rukhsara's is focused on the survival of her people, and the realm is only an incidental concern for her. Leviathan took a thousand-year sabbatical from the war. Sha's Oka is so fascinated/broken by the mystical nature of the Caul that he has trouble communicating to his troops. Feather Drenched in the Blood of the Fallen is more concerned with Sidereals. And Aqadar doesn't even care that he lives in the middle of a realm satrapy. <br /> <br /> Also, I think it's important that the fatsplat portray a coherent set of themes and a lunar society which newbies can understand quickly and play with. A broader vision should go in other supplements, like how Arms of the Chosen had a lot of fluff on lunar heroes that had nothing to do with the Silver Pact.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T17:09:37-08:00","id":1288441,"title":"","content":"Yeah...the impression I get is that most Lunars in the Pact at least pay lip service to the idea the Realm must go. Official, the Silver Pact claims this must extend to all the Shogunate successors, but that varies in it's interpretation. Remember those two Lunars who but heads over the defensive pact in the Hundred Kingdoms? Ones for because it will strengthen independence of the kingdoms, making it harder for the Realm to try and annexe them, the other objects because it empowers Lookshy?<br /> <br /> Not too mention, the further you are from the Realm and it's satrapys, the easier it is to condemn the Realm and then go about your day to day life, while taking no action. I mean these are the people who send hit squads after you and tell everyone you are a monster. Hell, I think that is exactly what the three 1st age elders in the shahan-yas (Raksi, Ma-Ha-Such and Leviathan) did. Leviathan spent most of his time depressed and not being particularly active in the Pact, but still hates the Realm and says so. Both Ma-Ha-Such and Raksi appear to be having a hissy fit over the 'endgame' of the Pact, but they aren't exactly under threat from the Legions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though to be fair, there is a chance that their step back from current affairs screams to me that it was Council censure. I just can't shake the idea that the argument got so bad the other shahan-yas told them to drop it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 02-18-2019, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T17:17:57-08:00","id":1288444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288347#post1288347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get it. The core book describing in explicit detail that there are Lunars, a decent number of them, that weren't affiliated with the Pact was one of the first things that stood out to me, and it seems to be widely overlooked elsewhere.<br /> <br /> The Lunars book contains frequent references to them, more than I'd have called for had it been my decision (I would have been wrong), and it's alternately not enough or just kind of missed?<br /> <br /> Wh- what more do people want? In terms of internal logic and gameplay and setting design, there's reasonable purpose behind the Silver Pact being prominent. What else can be done with the margins besides pointing out they exist, describing a bit of how they relate from a distance to the Pact, and dotting examples of people like that across the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping we see more as the text continues to be released, but how many concrete examples do we really get? This Chapter <i>is</i> titled &quot;The Silver Pact,&quot; I'll grant, but there doesn't seem to be another chapter coming up that gives focus to non-Pact Lunars, unless they're in the Quick Characters. What we have includes a good bit of general talk about how you aren't forced to join the Pact, and indeed how you can end up excluded from the Pact, but most of the Pact-peripheral Lunars mentioned are in fact technically members to some degree or other, and are elders to boot.<br /> <br /> Ul the Burning Eye, for instance, is said to tell would-be students that the Realm is &quot;a diversion from the Pact\u2019s true aims,&quot; indicating that he considers his estrangement from the Pact a &quot;No True Scotsman&quot; situation and himself an exemplar of the true cause. The Shadow-Fang Vanguard definitely aren't members, but they're still focused on opposition to the Realm and still have social ties to the Pact.<br /> <br /> Merchant-prince Hibiscus Cutter is the only named character I can point to in the material we've been shown so far who's <i>both</i> definitely not a member and has goals unrelated to the Realm. Even with Lilith it's said that a number of Pact Lunars still consider her a member even though she's completely cut herself off from human life.<br /> <br /> Now, what I <i>will</i> concede is that there are several established Pact Lunars whose <i>top</i> priority is something other than the Realm. Anja Silverclaws' focus on Mask of Winters, Tangaxoan's focus on bringing freedom to Ixcoatli, etcetera. That's a genuinely good answer to the &quot;mono-focused&quot; criticism.<br /> <br /> What I'd like to see and I'm not seeing is a Casteless Lunar with a philosophical opposition to the Pact, a la Madame Vert in 2E... though hopefully not pictured as a lizard with boobs. I'm not saying I want that stance to be common, and I <i>know</i> the text already generally acknowledges that you can write a character who fits that role without Creation imploding, I'd just like to see one case study illustrating it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T17:26:27-08:00","id":1288446,"title":"","content":"[sampling bias intensifies]<br /> <br /> Next chapter is Lunar Dominions, folks, I\u2019m sure we\u2019ll get a good few of those with minimal Pact interaction and nothing to do with the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T17:36:13-08:00","id":1288448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288446#post1288446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[sampling bias intensifies]<br /> <br /> Next chapter is Lunar Dominions, folks, I\u2019m sure we\u2019ll get a good few of those with minimal Pact interaction and nothing to do with the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll see but I'm not too sure given that every lunar elder was explicitly focusing on the Realm in some way or form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T18:13:03-08:00","id":1288459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288446#post1288446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[sampling bias intensifies]<br /> <br /> Next chapter is Lunar Dominions, folks, I\u2019m sure we\u2019ll get a good few of those with minimal Pact interaction and nothing to do with the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, a &quot;Dominion&quot; is a Pact structure. But, the Silver Pact chapter listed Shadow-Fang Vanguard members as shahan-yas, so... *shrugs* Maybe some of the Dominions won't really be Dominions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T18:17:27-08:00","id":1288460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288444#post1288444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'd like to see and I'm not seeing is a Casteless Lunar with a philosophical opposition to the Pact, a la Madame Vert in 2E... though hopefully not pictured as a lizard with boobs. I'm not saying I want that stance to be common, and I <i>know</i> the text already generally acknowledges that you can write a character who fits that role without Creation imploding, I'd just like to see one case study illustrating it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how the developers have described being Casteless, I would be surprised if there wasn't at least one in the chapter. The motivation would probably be different, as the tattoos specifically don't come with an obligation. Really, something like Vert's motive (if not her fervency) seems like the basic standard for an independent Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T03:17:28-08:00","id":1288559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288213#post1288213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not terribly concerned.<br /> The Silver Pact's general direction doesn\u2019t need to matter to any games any more than what the Lunars who aren\u2019t part of the PCs pack think is more important and it's a slightly more palatable answer than &quot;I'd love to help you with the Mask of Winters sport, but I'm three generations into turning a caste system into a meritocracy and if I don't micromanage I come back and the whole place is on fire, you know how it is?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, also.<br /> War against the Wyld is potentially more satisfying it'd also be difficult without a Fair Folk book. A lot of people don't even know about the direction they took in late 2e and have notions of them which are still heavily informed by Keychain of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T08:01:14-08:00","id":1288600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288448#post1288448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll see but I'm not too sure given that every lunar elder was explicitly focusing on the Realm in some way or form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Lunar elder <i>detailed in the chapter about the organization that fights the Realm</i> was explicitly focusing on the Realm in some way or form. On the other hand, one specific Lunar from the First Age got name-checked under the &quot;Independent Lunars&quot; heading at the end of that chapter as someone who left the Pact behind, so we explicitly know that not all Lunar elders are focusing on the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","user":"Verzio","date":".  Clarification 02-16-2019, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T09:24:45-08:00","id":1288623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288600#post1288600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Lunar elder <i>detailed in the chapter about the organization that fights the Realm</i> was explicitly focusing on the Realm in some way or form. On the other hand, one specific Lunar from the First Age got name-checked under the &amp;quot;Independent Lunars&amp;quot; heading at the end of that chapter as someone who left the Pact behind, so we explicitly know that not all Lunar elders are focusing on the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lilith is an independent lunar who seems to have no dominion. So we'd have to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T10:05:30-08:00","id":1288631,"title":"","content":"I don't have high expectations of the dominions chapter referring to Lunars with little or no conflict with the Realm (although I can make an argument for including at least one), but I definitely think it would be a less good chapter of it focused too heavily on the dominions of elders.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that I think referring to anybody fewer than five hundred years old as an elder in this context is a little bit silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T13:27:03-08:00","id":1288710,"title":"","content":"Responding directly to the question posed by the thread: I suppose it depends on what you think Lunars are <i>about</i>. I mean, obviously, one could say they're about a lot of things, but if we look roughly at what they represent and advance within the setting, compared to other released Exalt-types...<br /> <br /> To me, Solars are mostly about <i>improving things</i>. Given that improvement is extremely subjective, Solar games focus heavily on what can be fixed, what should be encouraged, and what should be destroyed. The Realm is clearly broken, but Solar opinions may differ on whether it's worth salvaging. Deconstruction requires games to challenge what it means for things to be &quot;better.&quot;<br /> <br /> To me, Dragon-Blooded are mostly about <i>legacy.</i> It's natural for short-lived mortals to want to leave a better world for their offspring than they had, and it's natural for this to lead to conflict with other clashing legacies, including changes wrought by younger generations, who see things very differently. Dragon-Blooded expand this conflict, and explore the fact that power hoarded across generations becomes a tyrannical force, which requires more and more work to maintain. Deconstruction requires games to challenge whether securing a legacy is worth the price paid.<br /> <br /> To me, Lunars are mostly about <i>freedom, </i>to be who and what they want, and to relate to the world in a way that suits them. But freedom is personalized, and sometimes groups of people acting in good faith have ways of life that are mutually exclusive. The privileged enjoy rare freedoms, whether earned by oppressing others under the guise of fair competition or divine right. Lunars have incredible freedoms, enough to allow them to see life from a variety of vantage points, and determine whether it's worth risking their own freedom to secure freedom for others. Deconstruction requires games to challenge who deserves freedom, given that so many cultures' definitions of freedom are incompatible.<br /> <br /> Given all of this, that the Realm (a tight-knit, oppressive, collectivist culture) is fundamentally inimical to what Lunars (a loosely-organized, laissez-faire, individualist culture) are about, and that it takes up half the known world, it would be strange if the Lunars focused less on the Realm than they do. They exist in the game (not necessarily in the setting) to challenge what the Realm stands for, and if we shied away from that, we'd end up with, well, the classic &quot;but what do Lunars actually <i>do</i>?&quot; question. A game about freedom doesn't really mean all that much without it being challenged, and without being encouraged to advance it in-setting.<br /> <br /> If this feels like a monofocus (particularly since attention has been specifically paid to talking about the Lunars who don't fit into this paradigm), then it would seem likely that the OP has a different understanding of what Dragon-Blooded and/or Lunars are about than I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 02-16-2019, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T15:08:31-08:00","id":1288751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288710#post1288710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given all of this, that the Realm (a tight-knit, oppressive, collectivist culture) is fundamentally inimical to what Lunars (a loosely-organized, laissez-faire, individualist culture) are about, and that it takes up half the known world, it would be strange if the Lunars focused less on the Realm than they do. They exist in the game (not necessarily in the setting) to challenge what the Realm stands for, and if we shied away from that, we'd end up with, well, the classic &quot;but what do Lunars actually <i>do</i>?&quot; question. A game about freedom doesn't really mean all that much without it being challenged, and without being encouraged to advance it in-setting.<br /> <br /> If this feels like a monofocus (particularly since attention has been specifically paid to talking about the Lunars who don't fit into this paradigm), then it would seem likely that the OP has a different understanding of what Dragon-Blooded and/or Lunars are about than I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe if you read my original post I was interested in seeing information about Lunars in locations remote from the Realm and how the Lunar culture there might have developed resulting in different organizations or focus. I was less interested in theme and rather in geography, if that is not what came across than that is a error on my part in my writing rather than intention. I do agree about freedom being a Lunar theme among others. Hopefully my interests will be satisfied in the dominion chapter instead since as others have pointed out right now all we have is the silver pack section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T15:36:11-08:00","id":1288760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288710#post1288710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Responding directly to the question posed by the thread: I suppose it depends on what you think Lunars are <i>about</i>. I mean, obviously, one could say they're about a lot of things, but if we look roughly at what they represent and advance within the setting, compared to other released Exalt-types...<br /> <br /> To me, Solars are mostly about <i>improving things</i>. Given that improvement is extremely subjective, Solar games focus heavily on what can be fixed, what should be encouraged, and what should be destroyed. The Realm is clearly broken, but Solar opinions may differ on whether it's worth salvaging. Deconstruction requires games to challenge what it means for things to be &amp;quot;better.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> To me, Dragon-Blooded are mostly about <i>legacy.</i> It's natural for short-lived mortals to want to leave a better world for their offspring than they had, and it's natural for this to lead to conflict with other clashing legacies, including changes wrought by younger generations, who see things very differently. Dragon-Blooded expand this conflict, and explore the fact that power hoarded across generations becomes a tyrannical force, which requires more and more work to maintain. Deconstruction requires games to challenge whether securing a legacy is worth the price paid.<br /> <br /> To me, Lunars are mostly about <i>freedom, </i>to be who and what they want, and to relate to the world in a way that suits them. But freedom is personalized, and sometimes groups of people acting in good faith have ways of life that are mutually exclusive. The privileged enjoy rare freedoms, whether earned by oppressing others under the guise of fair competition or divine right. Lunars have incredible freedoms, enough to allow them to see life from a variety of vantage points, and determine whether it's worth risking their own freedom to secure freedom for others. Deconstruction requires games to challenge who deserves freedom, given that so many cultures' definitions of freedom are incompatible.<br /> <br /> Given all of this, that the Realm (a tight-knit, oppressive, collectivist culture) is fundamentally inimical to what Lunars (a loosely-organized, laissez-faire, individualist culture) are about, and that it takes up half the known world, it would be strange if the Lunars focused less on the Realm than they do. They exist in the game (not necessarily in the setting) to challenge what the Realm stands for, and if we shied away from that, we'd end up with, well, the classic &amp;quot;but what do Lunars actually <i>do</i>?&amp;quot; question. A game about freedom doesn't really mean all that much without it being challenged, and without being encouraged to advance it in-setting.<br /> <br /> If this feels like a monofocus (particularly since attention has been specifically paid to talking about the Lunars who don't fit into this paradigm), then it would seem likely that the OP has a different understanding of what Dragon-Blooded and/or Lunars are about than I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh; the old World of Darkness arguments were before my time, but I've heard some accounts after the fact, and something in this line of discussion feels very reminiscent of them.<br /> <br /> Malcolm Sheppard may not be writing in this Lunars book, but I feel as though he is with it in spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288751#post1288751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was less interested in theme and rather in geography</div> </div> </div> </div>In a world where the landscape is neatly divided into five collective elementally-flavoured biomes, geography is but a mere kowtowing servant to theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T16:04:37-08:00","id":1288771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288751#post1288751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe if you read my original post I was interested in seeing information about Lunars in locations remote from the Realm and how the Lunar culture there might have developed resulting in different organizations or focus. I was less interested in theme and rather in geography, if that is not what came across than that is a error on my part in my writing rather than intention. I do agree about freedom being a Lunar theme among others. Hopefully my interests will be satisfied in the dominion chapter instead since as others have pointed out right now all we have is the silver pack section.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did see your post, but focused much more on the title and what I saw from a few responses in the thread. I apologize if I thus misread your intent!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T16:36:12-08:00","id":1288777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288710#post1288710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given all of this, that the Realm (a tight-knit, oppressive, collectivist culture) is fundamentally inimical to what Lunars (a loosely-organized, laissez-faire, individualist culture) are about, and that it takes up half the known world, it would be strange if the Lunars focused less on the Realm than they do. They exist in the game (not necessarily in the setting) to challenge what the Realm stands for, and if we shied away from that, we'd end up with, well, the classic &quot;but what do Lunars actually <i>do</i>?&quot; question. A game about freedom doesn't really mean all that much without it being challenged, and without being encouraged to advance it in-setting.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>For an exalt that represents freedom they seem to be chained by a war with the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T16:49:08-08:00","id":1288781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288777#post1288777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an exalt that represents freedom they seem to be chained by a war with the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly right. You've picked up the irony that makes Lunars suitable for the Age of Sorrows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T16:51:50-08:00","id":1288782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288781#post1288781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly right. You've picked up the irony that makes Lunars suitable for the Age of Sorrows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes it works sometimes I feel beings like Raksi's old edition look where she doesn't give a shit about anything other than learning more magic to be a much interesting take.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T18:45:12-08:00","id":1288800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288777#post1288777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an exalt that represents freedom they seem to be chained by a war with the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels very reminiscent of the fallacy of intolerance to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T20:55:40-08:00","id":1288832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288777#post1288777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an exalt that represents freedom they seem to be chained by a war with the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f4Mc-NYPHaQ\" data-code=\"f4Mc-NYPHaQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/f4Mc-NYPHaQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T21:13:32-08:00","id":1288834,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean, the circularity of the reasoning... I imagine that many Lunars who desire freedom view conflict with the Realm confining, and find the most effective way to break out of that confinement to be making the Realm not a thing anymore.<br /> <br /> What exactly is clever bollocks Lunar who points out the supposed contradiction offering as an alternative form of supposedly purer freedom?<br /> <br /> &quot;We're fighting the Nazis because we want them to stop killing people.&quot;<br /> &quot;But fighting Nazis gives them an opportunity to kill people! Plot hole DING!!!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T22:59:38-08:00","id":1288856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288760#post1288760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a world where the landscape is neatly divided into five collective elementally-flavoured biomes, geography is but a mere kowtowing servant to theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods, next you will be bringing up that some people can just summon clouds and tornadoes to ride around on to go wherever they want ;_;<br /> <br /> I guess for such a large world Creation can be very small?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T04:57:54-08:00","id":1288898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288856#post1288856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gods, next you will be bringing up that some people can just summon clouds and tornadoes to ride around on to go wherever they want ;_;<br /> <br /> I guess for such a large world Creation can be very small?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not supposed to be which is a problem. The realm is a superpower but it doesn't control everything. Lunars don't have a centralized power base but apparently they still meet with each other on a constant basis. I have no problem with the silver pact being about fighting the realm. I do have an issue with every lunar putting any other goals aside to do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-17-2019, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T05:15:00-08:00","id":1288902,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't think that &quot;to be focused on realm&quot; is a bad thing as is. But it's important HOW they gonna destroy it. Personally I hoped for Lunars - progressist evolutionists and social engineers who try to create a new societies more powerful than the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T06:40:13-08:00","id":1288908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288898#post1288898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have an issue with every lunar putting any other goals aside to do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty serious exaggeration of the details we've been given.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T06:56:39-08:00","id":1288915,"title":"","content":"Less an exaggeration, more &quot;explicitly contradicted by the text&quot;<br /> <br /> Anya Silverclaws don't give two shits about the realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T08:00:51-08:00","id":1288923,"title":"","content":"I'm going to have to check the text out, but Lunars as warriors for freedom and individuality (with its unfortunate overtones of Hollywood style William Wallace) seems at odds with the discussion that Lunars vs the Realm is pretty much all solely about revenge, removing a personal threat and an ideology free beef with the Dragonblooded in particular? (Actually the whole thing I thought 3e was trying to do with the Lunars was remove any ideology that the players would find questionable or doubtful in particular.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T09:41:24-08:00","id":1288935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288923#post1288923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to check the text out, but Lunars as warriors for freedom and individuality (with its unfortunate overtones of Hollywood style William Wallace) seems at odds with the discussion that Lunars vs the Realm is pretty much all solely about revenge, removing a personal threat and an ideology free beef with the Dragonblooded in particular? (Actually the whole thing I thought 3e was trying to do with the Lunars was remove any ideology that the players would find questionable or doubtful in particular.)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;While the Dragon-Blooded successors to the Shogunate are the Silver Pact\u2019s foremost enemies,<br /> only its most extremist members extend this to all the Terrestrial Exalted. Dragon-Blooded<br /> societies that don\u2019t claim descent from the hated Shogunate or engage in imperialist ventures are<br /> considered a different breed, and though they may not be fully trusted, they can be valuable allies<br /> to the Pact.&quot;<br /> <br /> And a direct passage says that the Lunars don&quot;t have a beef with all Dragonblooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T11:26:56-08:00","id":1288956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288923#post1288923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to check the text out, but Lunars as warriors for freedom and individuality</div> </div> </div> </div> I do not believe that Dex Davican said that they're fighting (on the whole) for the freedom of anybody besides themselves. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(with its unfortunate overtones of Hollywood style William Wallace)</div> </div> </div> </div> Braveheart is kind of silly, but so are a lot of the contrary hot takes that Scottish wars of independence were unconcerned with any form or standard of the term. Historically, a lot of people have fought for preferences of one kind of overlord compared to another.<br /> <br /> A lot of American revolutionaries had the audacity to refer to themselves as slaves, even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-17-2019, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T12:48:56-08:00","id":1288982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288923#post1288923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to check the text out, but Lunars as warriors for freedom and individuality (with its unfortunate overtones of Hollywood style William Wallace) seems at odds with the discussion that Lunars vs the Realm is pretty much all solely about revenge, removing a personal threat and an ideology free beef with the Dragonblooded in particular? (Actually the whole thing I thought 3e was trying to do with the Lunars was remove any ideology that the players would find questionable or doubtful in particular.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that Lunars are warriors for freedom and individuality. I said that they're <i>about freedom</i>. As a part of the setting, Lunars are the group best suited to games that explore themes of freedom--what freedom means, who deserves it, what it's like to lose it, and what you do with it when you have it. <i>Many</i> Lunars lean into these themes and become warriors for freedom and individuality, but the Raksi/Ma-Ha-Suchi schism showcases how that's not a simple thing to define. They both want a world without the Realm's oppression, but they disagree on what role Lunars should play in the aftermath. And many other Lunars choose to fight to maintain only their personal freedoms, or run away from responsibility, or simply enjoy life to its fullest.<br /> <br /> Revenge Against The Machine is a terrible cover band name. Revenge may motivate many elders, and may motivate a significant number of younger Lunars, but the keyword is <i>rage</i>. Lunars in the Age of Sorrows are divine tricksters who break what would cage them, and change themselves to frustrate and evade what they can't break. Many, but not all, are enraged on behalf of others as well. Lunars upset the established order because they're good at it and it needs doing, and when that's done, they'll figure out what happens next. (Also, &quot;revenge&quot; is not ideology-free beef.)<br /> <br /> No idea who told you that &quot;Lunars without any ideology that players might find questionable or doubtful&quot; was any kind of goal the game might have. The Silver Pact is a society, and societies by nature have ideologies. More importantly, games require structures and goals to either play toward or against. Lunars have more in-setting freedom to play against type than, say, Dynasts, but if we go too far in in the interest of giving <i>players</i> more freedom, we'll run into What Do Lunars Even Do, mk. 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T14:18:43-08:00","id":1288997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm#post1288173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess what I am saying is why should the medicine man of a far north eastern tribe care about some empire he only vaguely knows of compared to fighting cruel winter gods, heartless fair-folk with skin of ice, and strange beasts born under a strange sign in the sky? Perhaps I am being overly finicky but I think it would have been interesting to explore those groups detached from struggle against the realm, even if only a small paragraph or one to two examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly you're not totally wrong here. It's absolutely reasonable that people living on the edge of the Threshold have other concerns. That's kind of what defines the Threshold: the Realm's influence is progressively more distant the further from the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> It's totally cool to run that kind of campaign. For example, were I ever to play in a Dragon-blood game I'd ideally play a Wanasaan - an Outcaste with no connection to the Realm. You can have the same with Lunars, too.<br /> <br /> To be fair to the counterpoint, though? The Realm goes out of its way to hunt you down because of what you are. As a mortal you might not have had any qualms with the Realm, but now they're hunting you to kill you til you're dead. That's a huge reason why many new Lunars join the Pact: the Realm is picking sides for them. Even at the deepest ends of the Threshold I can imagine the local city-states and tribes warily providing hospitality to a band of the Wyld Hunt, not needing to ask them what brings such foreigners to such distant lands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T14:58:57-08:00","id":1289002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288997#post1288997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair to the counterpoint, though? The Realm goes out of its way to hunt you down because of what you are. As a mortal you might not have had any qualms with the Realm, but now they're hunting you to kill you til you're dead. That's a huge reason why many new Lunars join the Pact: the Realm is picking sides for them. Even at the deepest ends of the Threshold I can imagine the local city-states and tribes warily providing hospitality to a band of the Wyld Hunt, not needing to ask them what brings such foreigners to such distant lands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, arguably the biggest reason why the deepest ends of the Threshold aren't already satrapies is due to the efforts of the Silver Pact. You <i>can</i> fuck off to the ass-end of nowhere, but a case can be made that you have that ability largely because of the efforts of your peers. If enough Lunars go the Subtle Lunar Sabbatical route, they will subsequently lose that ability. Or they would have, before the Time of Tumult. A lot of things are in the air now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T15:10:43-08:00","id":1289007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289002#post1289002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, arguably the biggest reason why the deepest ends of the Threshold aren't already satrapies is due to the efforts of the Silver Pact. You <i>can</i> fuck off to the ass-end of nowhere, but a case can be made that you have that ability largely because of the efforts of your peers. If enough Lunars go the Subtle Lunar Sabbatical route, they will subsequently lose that ability. Or they would have, before the Time of Tumult. A lot of things are in the air now.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that wasn't the case before. The Realm's boundaries used to exist due to the fact that the realm has limits. Maintaining an empire as big as it is takes effort and spreading it out even further would have just caused a collapse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T15:14:12-08:00","id":1289009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289007#post1289007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that wasn't the case before. The Realm's boundaries used to exist due to the fact that the realm has limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between Dragon Blooded Charms and assumptions about Artifacts, the limits of the Realm in the absence of Lunars have changed, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T15:19:21-08:00","id":1289013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289009#post1289009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Between Dragon Blooded Charms and assumptions about Artifacts, the limits of the Realm in the absence of Lunars have changed, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? Because it seems to me that creation is much better than before and it's amazing to believe that only ten thousand dragon blooded could actually keep that much ground together. I feel like the writers have made creation bigger without realizing just how far things are now. The limits of the realm are more of an issue now more than ever.<br /> <br /> Like Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi are on opposite ends of each other in the east. The map is so massive how the hell do they even meet up without charms. How do the lunar elders meet up so constantly despite the being tens of thousands of miles apart?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T15:36:18-08:00","id":1289021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288982#post1288982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, &quot;revenge&quot; is not ideology-free beef.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think you'd be pushing at the limits of the term to describe &quot;revenge&quot; as ideology. There's perhaps a sense in which &quot;I must find the man who killed my father... Prepare to die!&quot; or &quot;Win back the lands unjustly robbed from us by unfair treaties&quot; or &quot;I should be the caliph instead of the caliph!&quot; are ideology.<br /> <br /> But clearly in a very different sense from &quot;Civilization is a complex machine, doomed to failure states&quot;, &quot;Hierarchy is immoral&quot;, &quot;Property is theft&quot; and the like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1288982#post1288982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No idea who told you that &quot;Lunars without any ideology that players might find questionable or doubtful&quot; was any kind of goal the game might have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not something I've been told, as such, but certainly an inference from the early 3e devs talking about the problems of ideological barbarism, which 1e and 2e presented in different ways - 1e from a sort of perspective of anarchist resistance to the hierarchies and division of labour in civilization, 2e from a perspective of the Thousand Streams River as a sort of champion of encouraging and sowing cultural diversity as strengthening humanity. Anarchist barbarians, cultural diversity barbarians, anti-imperialism barbarians.<br /> <br /> 3e's intention, as I understood it, was to cut through the idea that the Silver Pact was in a sense an ideologically motivated vehicle opposed to civilization. It doesn't seem like a good idea, then, to in any way recreate a conflict around the Silver Pact having an ideological conflict with anything the Realm represents as the force of imperial civilization (that seems like going back to anarchist barbarians again).<br /> <br /> This frankly this is all kind of tangential though, as after rereading and these comments, I understand better now that you were talking not about a conscious ideology inclined to prize freedom among the Lunar Exalted, as I'd thought, but more that they and the Dragonblooded Realm represent opposing themes which should be brought into clash. That said, I do disagree that this is actually a good lens to bring to stories involving both and conflicts between them though, or useful themes to hang on these splats and factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T17:19:23-08:00","id":1289037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289007#post1289007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that wasn't the case before. The Realm's boundaries used to exist due to the fact that the realm has limits. Maintaining an empire as big as it is takes effort and spreading it out even further would have just caused a collapse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it changed. Because &quot;we've been hiding for over a millennium, should we maybe do something?&quot; and &quot;I want to build a better society, but the expansionist military regime keeps declaring war on me and/or assassinating my friends for doing so&quot; are way worse starting points for a game. As we've seen, following two editions of complaints about Lunars.<br /> <br /> And because when we look at what &quot;the Realm has limits&quot; really means, I think we can recognize that when part of an expansionist military regime &quot;collapses&quot; due to &quot;spreading out&quot; too far, that generally looks like a bloody rebellion, a bloody conquest from an outside power, or a failed conquest of a would-be satrapy (or, sometimes, brutal pogroms that leave nothing left to govern). Though the Realm has significant corruption problems, much of what outsiders would view as corruption is the system working as intended from a Dynastic perspective, because the outside world is rightfully theirs for the despoiling. An expansionist military regime recognizes its limits in terms of what it can't yet conquer, and recognizes problems like corruption, poor communication, and resource shortages as impediments to total military/spiritual domination.<br /> <br /> &quot;An empire ruled by ten thousand demigods can't conquer a world mostly full of mortals and maintain cohesion&quot; is a thought-provoking and harrowing statement about the limitations of centralized control and the challenges of bureaucracy, but it left the Lunars doing nothing in particular on the world stage for fifteen hundred years, and it frankly makes the Realm seem like a paper tiger waiting for the Celestial Exalted to come knock it over. I think &quot;An empire ruled by ten thousand demigods can't conquer a world full of mortals when undercut by the persistent sabotage of reincarnating culture-hero demigods&quot; makes for a more interesting game for players of Dragon-Blooded and Lunars both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This frankly this is all kind of tangential though, as after rereading and these comments, I understand better now that you were talking not about a conscious ideology inclined to prize freedom among the Lunar Exalted, as I'd thought, but more that they and the Dragonblooded Realm represent opposing themes which should be brought into clash. </div> </div> </div>There's definite overlap between what I think a Lunar game is about and what Lunar society on average believes in. Lunars are suited to being freedom-fighters, they're all given personal attention and reinforcement of their identity by their iconoclastic patron, their first experiences with peers will likely encourage them to interact with the Silver Pact, and they all have reason to fear the loss of their own freedoms (whether freedom to worship, maintain their way of life, or simply survive) at the hands of the Realm, so it makes sense to gravitate toward that life. But none of them are <i>required</i> to live that life, and can play against type with relatively few consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I do disagree that this is actually a good lens to bring to stories involving both and conflicts between them though, or useful themes to hang on these splats and factions. </div> </div> </div>This really interests me. Why is this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T17:26:40-08:00","id":1289040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289013#post1289013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How? Because it seems to me that creation is much better than before and it's amazing to believe that only ten thousand dragon blooded could actually keep that much ground together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presuming the Realm's boundaries in the Threshold were as they were in Second Edition, how do you picture the Dragon Blooded (10000 Dynasts plus a few thousand recruited outcastes) being distributed through it?<br /> <br /> Creation is bigger, but a lot of that is at the borders. Most stuff is no further away from the Blessed Isle than it used to be.<br /> <br /> The Western archipelagos are the exception and the settings history has been adjusted to account for that. As for how the Realm would exert power there if undeterred by Lunars, presumably in a similar manner to Portugal exerting power at points of the African coast thousands of miles and several months away by ship; systemized annual voyages, recruiting local intermediaries, instituting garrisons and leveraging superior firepower.<br /> <br /> Imagine a group that could extend a land empire as far as the Mongols, but with greater cohesion in the ruling class to ensure uniformity.<br /> <br /> I'll note that the portrayal of the extent of the Realm's power from First Edition, while internally logical, was still something precisely engineered to serve providing a setting for Solar games. Those writers could have come up with something with more reach and stronger control, but Grabowski viewed such as being discouraging for Solar intrigue and adventure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi are on opposite ends of each other in the east. The map is so massive how the hell do they even meet up without charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why on earth would they want to?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the lunar elders meet up so constantly despite the being tens of thousands of miles apart?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that number is exaggerated.<br /> <br /> Do you know how many varieties of bird can fly non-stop for thousands of miles of migration?<br /> <br /> I wonder what kinds of Charms for speed Lunars are going to get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T17:36:11-08:00","id":1289042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289037#post1289037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it changed. Because &quot;we've been hiding for over a millennium, should we maybe do something?&quot; and &quot;I want to build a better society, but the expansionist military regime keeps declaring war on me and/or assassinating my friends for doing so&quot; are way worse starting points for a game. As we've seen, following two editions of complaints about Lunars.<br /> <br /> And because when we look at what &quot;the Realm has limits&quot; really means, I think we can recognize that when part of an expansionist military regime &quot;collapses&quot; due to &quot;spreading out&quot; too far, that generally looks like a bloody rebellion, a bloody conquest from an outside power, or a failed conquest of a would-be satrapy (or, sometimes, brutal pogroms that leave nothing left to govern). Though the Realm has significant corruption problems, much of what outsiders would view as corruption is the system working as intended from a Dynastic perspective, because the outside world is rightfully theirs for the despoiling. An expansionist military regime recognizes its limits in terms of what it can't yet conquer, and recognizes problems like corruption, poor communication, and resource shortages as impediments to total military/spiritual domination.<br /> <br /> &quot;An empire ruled by ten thousand demigods can't conquer a world mostly full of mortals and maintain cohesion&quot; is a thought-provoking and harrowing statement about the limitations of centralized control and the challenges of bureaucracy, but it left the Lunars doing nothing in particular on the world stage for fifteen hundred years, and it frankly makes the Realm seem like a paper tiger waiting for the Celestial Exalted to come knock it over. I think &quot;An empire ruled by ten thousand demigods can't conquer a world full of mortals when undercut by the persistent sabotage of reincarnating culture-hero demigods&quot; makes for a more interesting game for players of Dragon-Blooded and Lunars both.<br /> <br /> There's definite overlap between what I think a Lunar game is about and what Lunar society on average believes in. Lunars are suited to being freedom-fighters, they're all given personal attention and reinforcement of their identity by their iconoclastic patron, their first experiences with peers will likely encourage them to interact with the Silver Pact, and they all have reason to fear the loss of their own freedoms (whether freedom to worship, maintain their way of life, or simply survive) at the hands of the Realm, so it makes sense to gravitate toward that life. But none of them are <i>required</i> to live that life, and can play against type with relatively few consequences.<br /> <br /> This really interests me. Why is this?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that dragon blooded at those numbers don't have the ability to coordinate effectively. This is less about centralizing power and more about the fact that that dragon blooded have limits and with the size of creation changing, the realm Dragon blooded numbers cannot realistically be at only at ten thousand. This also relates to the issue with the threshold because there's no real way for dragon blooded to have enough troops to prevent the strapies from rebelling, even with legions at hand. The space to cover and the times of mobility would make it impossible to control it all. As well as the distance between them makes what the dragon blooded even have hard to maintain.<br /> <br /> This all relates to the point of how the lunars have been actually dealing with the realm because logistically, even mortals with their own cultures who have their own troops would be able to rebel down the line. Lunars shouldn't be having much of an issue with most of this. The dragon blooded outside of a super weapon the empress couldn't casually wield just don't have the ability to grow at their numbers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T18:23:37-08:00","id":1289048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289042#post1289042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that dragon blooded at those numbers don't have the ability to coordinate effectively. This is less about centralizing power and more about the fact that that dragon blooded have limits and with the size of creation changing, the realm Dragon blooded numbers cannot realistically be at only at ten thousand. This also relates to the issue with the threshold because there's no real way for dragon blooded to have enough troops to prevent the strapies from rebelling, even with legions at hand. The space to cover and the times of mobility would make it impossible to control it all. As well as the distance between them makes what the dragon blooded even have hard to maintain.<br /> <br /> This all relates to the point of how the lunars have been actually dealing with the realm because logistically, even mortals with their own cultures who have their own troops would be able to rebel down the line. Lunars shouldn't be having much of an issue with most of this. The dragon blooded outside of a super weapon the empress couldn't casually wield just don't have the ability to grow at their numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that members of the team have put a lot of time and thought into getting numbers to be sensible, but as I wasn't one of those team members, I won't speak for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T19:15:52-08:00","id":1289060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289042#post1289042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that dragon blooded at those numbers don't have the ability to coordinate effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">with the size of creation changing, the realm Dragon blooded numbers cannot realistically be at only at ten thousand.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still seem to be looking at things in terms of a model where Realm government requires an even distribution of the Exalted, and that a lot of the imperialism needs to be concerned with the sparsely populated margins of Creation. The Inland Sea hasn't gotten any bigger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This also relates to the issue with the threshold because there's no real way for dragon blooded to have enough troops to prevent the strapies from rebelling, even with legions at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>This raises a few questions: why don't you think they can have enough troops? What do troops need to be for? What kinds of tactics do Realm legions employ, and might they often scare off rebellion before it happens?<br /> <br /> Look at Perfect Soul's homeland, and how much of the work of controlling and suppressing the populace was delegated to her ruling family. Look at Second Edition Greyfalls, where the Realm elevated a traditionally marginalized ethnic group over the others, making them motivated on several fronts to enforce Realm policy.<br /> <br /> The British Raj at times governed with an army in just the few hundred thousands over a population of tens of millions, and still rather far from the homeland.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The space to cover and the times of mobility would make it impossible to control it all.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the event that the more sophisticated instruments of empire fail, and an army needs to march, if it's not on the order of years then all the time benefits a rebellious satrapy might be time to enjoy themselves before the burning starts.<br /> <br /> Canals would help, if the Lunars didn't keep breaking them. Look what China did with canals.<br /> <br /> And hey, maybe an unmolested Realm could build in not-mountains the kind of continental road network that the Incas built in mountains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T19:40:17-08:00","id":1289063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289042#post1289042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that dragon blooded at those numbers don't have the ability to coordinate effectively. This is less about centralizing power and more about the fact that that dragon blooded have limits and with the size of creation changing, the realm Dragon blooded numbers cannot realistically be at only at ten thousand. This also relates to the issue with the threshold because there's no real way for dragon blooded to have enough troops to prevent the strapies from rebelling, even with legions at hand. The space to cover and the times of mobility would make it impossible to control it all. As well as the distance between them makes what the dragon blooded even have hard to maintain.<br /> <br /> This all relates to the point of how the lunars have been actually dealing with the realm because logistically, even mortals with their own cultures who have their own troops would be able to rebel down the line. Lunars shouldn't be having much of an issue with most of this. The dragon blooded outside of a super weapon the empress couldn't casually wield just don't have the ability to grow at their numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought there were ~30,000 DBs, am I wrong or are you speaking only about the realm-loyal DBs? I've felt for a while that Exalted's setting might make more sense if you multiplied the number of Exalted by 10, because as it currently stands the chances of 2 solars meeting is something close to 5%, let alone a full circle forming. This is making a lot of assumptions, the most incorrect being that there is no destiny pushing their chances of meeting higher. The sidereals in particular have trouble making sense to me, given their factional politics and wide-reaching influence, which I have dealt with by making the gods and god-blooded far bigger parts of their stories.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, with the solars, in particular, being like Heracles in terms of level of power and the world being generally bronze-age level tech perhaps the presence of even more of them would overwhelm everything in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T19:49:57-08:00","id":1289064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289048#post1289048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that members of the team have put a lot of time and thought into getting numbers to be sensible, but as I wasn't one of those team members, I won't speak for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That number has been going since 1e and before 3e it was much much smaller location. It made sense when the world was much smaller but it really doesn't now.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T19:50:59-08:00","id":1289065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nabirius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289063#post1289063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought there were ~30,000 DBs, am I wrong or are you speaking only about the realm-loyal DBs? I've felt for a while that Exalted's setting might make more sense if you multiplied the number of Exalted by 10, because as it currently stands the chances of 2 solars meeting is something close to 5%, let alone a full circle forming. This is making a lot of assumptions, the most incorrect being that there is no destiny pushing their chances of meeting higher. The sidereals in particular have trouble making sense to me, given their factional politics and wide-reaching influence, which I have dealt with by making the gods and god-blooded far bigger parts of their stories.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, with the solars, in particular, being like Heracles in terms of level of power and the world being generally bronze-age level tech perhaps the presence of even more of them would overwhelm everything in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are only 10k Realm-loyal DBs then about 15k DBs around the world.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T19:53:37-08:00","id":1289066,"title":"","content":"Oh I'm sorry, my previous statement about the British Raj was in error, made based on just a cursory examination.<br /> <br /> No, so in 1880, the standing army in the British Raj consisted of about 500,000 troops (more than half of which consisted of the distributed armies of various local princes), responsible for a population of <i>255 million people</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T20:00:09-08:00","id":1289067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289065#post1289065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are only 10k Realm-loyal DBs then about 15k DBs around the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're discounting the thousands of outcasts serving the Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289064#post1289064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That number has been going since 1e and before 3e it was much much smaller location. It made sense when the world was much smaller but it really doesn't now.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does the size of the world matter, when most of that is added to the edge?<br /> <br /> Mind, Prasad represents an interesting picture of how the Realm might have developed with more impunity to seize the Scavenger Lands and the West. That's another 2000 technically under the Realm umbrella.<br /> <br /> Suppose the Empress had tried to take the River Province again, with a committed campaign, and won. Lookshy is home to about 3000 Exalted. What is to be done with them in defeat, execution en masse? Or are they presumed to fight to the last person?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T20:08:46-08:00","id":1289069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289065#post1289065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are only 10k Realm-loyal DBs then about 15k DBs around the world.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are also 4000 lost eggs all of which on either in the imperial legions or the immaculate faith. They also have access to Cadet houses (750) and patricians (250) For a total of 15 000.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T20:19:48-08:00","id":1289071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289060#post1289060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You still seem to be looking at things in terms of a model where Realm government requires an even distribution of the Exalted, and that a lot of the imperialism needs to be concerned with the sparsely populated margins of Creation. The Inland Sea hasn't gotten any bigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>And also the lands around which have gotten bigger. Which matters more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This raises a few questions: why don't you think they can have enough troops? What do troops need to be for? What kinds of tactics do Realm legions employ, and might they often scare off rebellion before it happens?<br /> <br /> Look at Perfect Soul's homeland, and how much of the work of controlling and suppressing the populace was delegated to her ruling family. Look at Second Edition Greyfalls, where the Realm elevated a traditionally marginalized ethnic group over the others, making them motivated on several fronts to enforce Realm policy.<br /> <br /> The British Raj at times governed with an army in just the few hundred thousands over a population of tens of millions, and still rather far from the homeland. </div> </div> </div>Because of the way they managed to control India. It was a host of unique factors to lead to that situation. However, without dragon blooded to contain the situation there's a limit to what they can do. It depends on the culture and also the guild influence to counterbalance the dragon blooded. The problem is that we only have the current charms to dictate how the dragon blooded use their charms to interact with the world. Not to mention how individual dragon blooded work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the event that the more sophisticated instruments of empire fail, and an army needs to march, if it's not on the order of years then all the time benefits a rebellious satrapy might be time to enjoy themselves before the burning starts.<br /> <br /> Canals would help, if the Lunars didn't keep breaking them. Look what China did with canals.<br /> <br /> And hey, maybe an unmolested Realm could build in not-mountains the kind of continental road network that the Incas built in mountains. </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm mistaken the incas weren't dealing with a tract of land as large as the realm is. If I'm reading this right the blessed isle alone is about the size of china and the surrounding territories probably triple the size in terms of traveling from end to end. Granted they'd still use near by troops if they could afford it but that still doesn't seem like a feasible option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T20:23:58-08:00","id":1289072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289067#post1289067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're discounting the thousands of outcasts serving the Realm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What does the size of the world matter, when most of that is added to the edge?<br /> <br /> Mind, Prasad represents an interesting picture of how the Realm might have developed with more impunity to seize the Scavenger Lands and the West. That's another 2000 technically under the Realm umbrella.<br /> <br /> Suppose the Empress had tried to take the River Province again, with a committed campaign, and won. Lookshy is home to about 3000 Exalted. What is to be done with them in defeat, execution en masse? Or are they presumed to fight to the last person?</div> </div> </div> </div>Size matters because it determines supply lines, how well stocked the realm is to repel people from strapies and how far they can expand. When talking about other nations just a few exalts aren't going to cut it when it comes to controlling a sizable portion of land.<br /> <br /> I mean I would presume they'd have their leaders executed considering that a campaign would have cause the empress thousands of her own dragon blooded to win such a campaign. Even with sidereal influence, that's a campaign against independent dragon blooded, gods, and any other exalt that decided to help. The realm doesn't have limitless dragon blooded. So I forgot the other few thousands of dragon blooded. It feels like they'd need triple that number to effectively manage what's equal to a third of the world (factoring water)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-17-2019, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T20:33:06-08:00","id":1289073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289071#post1289071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And also the lands around which have gotten bigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because of the way they managed to control India. It was a host of unique factors to lead to that situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those situations couldn't exist in satrapies? Does Jiara not give a hint.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, without dragon blooded to contain the situation there's a limit to what they can do. It depends on the culture and also the guild influence to counterbalance the dragon blooded. The problem is that we only have the current charms to dictate how the dragon blooded use their charms to interact with the world. Not to mention how individual dragon blooded work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really figure out what this is saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I'm mistaken the incas weren't dealing with a tract of land as large as the realm is.</div> </div> </div> </div>{raise eyebrow}<br /> <br /> It would have been... so easy to just Google &quot;how long was the Inca road system&quot;. Taken about two seconds.<br /> <br /> The Inca road system, was forty <i>thousand <b> kilometres</b></i> long, and was built over <i><b>mountains</b></i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm reading this right the blessed isle alone is about the size of china and the surrounding territories probably triple the size in terms of traveling from end to end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, canals. China had a thousand mile long canal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted they'd still use near by troops if they could afford it but that still doesn't seem like a feasible option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T20:47:24-08:00","id":1289076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289073#post1289073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And those situations couldn't exist in satrapies? Does Jiara not give a hint.</div> </div> </div> </div>In some situations yes, sure. However, that was part of my next point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't really figure out what this is saying. </div> </div> </div>I'm getting tired but basically my point is that Exalts are limited by how much their charms limit them. And yes a dragon blooded can do a lot more than a mortal can; however, those charms don't quite give them enough to just control a nation a few charms in. The dragon-blooded can't just force a nation to bow under their will with just a few words like a lunar could with just a few charms. They need numbers and an army.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> {raise eyebrow}<br /> <br /> It would have been... so easy to just Google &quot;how long was the Inca road system&quot;. Taken about two seconds.<br /> <br /> The Inca road system, was forty <i>thousand <b> kilometres</b></i> long, and was built over <i><b>mountains</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Yeah, canals. China had a thousand mile long canal.<br /> <br /> Why not? </div> </div> </div>I mean I'm sure those would help but I was just referring to as you said the years it would take to reach from one place to another. The ability to hold the lands from valid threats and the people it would take to maintain the land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T21:29:32-08:00","id":1289085,"title":"","content":"The Realm doesn't need to put a hundred Dragon-Blooded into each satrapy to dominate it, is what Isator's saying. The Realm's structure of imperialism is one where they generally don't need to deal with disputes, because they bend the rulers of the satrapies to crush their own people <i>so the Dragon-Blooded and Legions don't even have to</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-18-2019, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T21:32:58-08:00","id":1289086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289085#post1289085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm doesn't need to put a hundred Dragon-Blooded into each satrapy to dominate it, is what Isator's saying. The Realm's structure of imperialism is one where they generally don't need to send legions to deal with disputes, because they bend the rulers of the satrapies to crush their own people <i>so they don't have to</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet also have to deal with things outside of the nation like the guild and other factions. The Realm can only work with that kind of pressure by have dragon-blooded on hand in order to make sure the system works the way it's supposed to. Especially the farther they go out of the threshold. This isn't even counting lunars. There are a lot threats that they have to worry about to actually be able to maintain what they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T21:42:56-08:00","id":1289089,"title":"","content":"The Realm isn't the one who has to worry about the Guild trying to sink its tendrils into a satrapy. The ruler of the satrapy is. If the system doesn't work the way it's supposed to, once it starts missing payments, <i>then</i> the Dragon-Blooded get involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-18-2019, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T21:49:57-08:00","id":1289090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289089#post1289089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm isn't the one who has to worry about the Guild trying to sink its tendrils into a satrapy. The ruler of the satrapy is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how far the guild already influences the area. There are too many factors outside of lunars. The guild, errant gods, hidden demon cults, other things which can make it a untenable to control the area.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T21:59:18-08:00","id":1289093,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I feel as though when a whole page of a thread is approaching the point of consisting solely of two posters back and forth, it's time to pack it in.<br /> <br /> Personally because I'd be more concerned at the implication that other participants are becoming bored and alienated than anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T22:02:19-08:00","id":1289094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289093#post1289093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I feel as though when a whole page of a thread is approaching the point of consisting solely of two posters back and forth, it's time to pack it in.<br /> <br /> Personally because I'd be more concerned at the implication that other participants are becoming bored and alienated than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T22:02:58-08:00","id":1289095,"title":"","content":"Mortals have very efficiently managed communities in the real world without needing Dragon-Blooded intervention. The various polities in the setting managed to do fine <i>without</i> Dragon-Blooded running them - why do they suddenly fall apart when Dragon-Blooded exist, but aren't directly pulling the levers of society?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T22:11:56-08:00","id":1289099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289095#post1289095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals have very efficiently managed communities in the real world without needing Dragon-Blooded intervention. The various polities in the setting managed to do fine <i>without</i> Dragon-Blooded running them - why do they suddenly fall apart when Dragon-Blooded exist, but aren't directly pulling the levers of society?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the farther you are from the blessed isle the more issues you run into. It's again, not just lunars that cause dragon blooded problems. There are hosts of other threats that would require direct dragon-blooded intervention. The real world doesn't have to deal with magic or spirits demanding tribute.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T22:32:54-08:00","id":1289100,"title":"","content":"And again, how did these mortal communities manage to deal with these supernatural threats before the Dragon-Blooded asked for a yearly tithe of jade? Because they managed it before; it's not like these bugaboos only emerged when the Realm showed up to tax them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-18-2019, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T22:51:28-08:00","id":1289105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is that dragon blooded at those numbers don't have the ability to coordinate effectively. This is less about centralizing power and more about the fact that that dragon blooded have limits and with the size of creation changing, the realm Dragon blooded numbers cannot realistically be at only at ten thousand. This also relates to the issue with the threshold because there's no real way for dragon blooded to have enough troops to prevent the strapies from rebelling, even with legions at hand. The space to cover and the times of mobility would make it impossible to control it all. As well as the distance between them makes what the dragon blooded even have hard to maintain. </div> </div> </div>This entire thing seems grounded in the assumption that the dragon blooded have to do everything themselves instead of having a lot of mortals under them that handle a lot of things involved in running the empire. Its not like they have to assign a dragon blooded to personally oversee every single mine, outpost, and etc in their empire.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just meant the part about how 10,000 dragon blooded aren't enough. Not the part about also not having armies big enough in general. 10,000 dragon blooded is plenty unless they are OCD control freaks that insist on micromanaging every single thing and having a dragon blooded assigned to every single operation instead of trusting mortals to run some things for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-18-2019, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T23:03:22-08:00","id":1289108,"title":"","content":"If mortals didn't have the strength, conviction, guile, smarts, or charisma to at least <i>occasionally</i> triumph against predations from the supernatural world, the setting just straight-up wouldn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T23:17:38-08:00","id":1289112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289100#post1289100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, how did these mortal communities manage to deal with these supernatural threats before the Dragon-Blooded asked for a yearly tithe of jade? Because they managed it before; it's not like these bugaboos only emerged when the Realm showed up to tax them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like harborhead which is much closer to the blessed isle than white wall or a bunch of other places which are screwed because strong gods take over an area? Mortals can get lucky or be incredibly screwed. You can't send someone as strong as Alhat or the syndicates against a mortal army. That's just an easy slaughter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T23:24:15-08:00","id":1289115,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that the Syndics of Whitewall and Ahlat in Harborhead have reached a sort of equilibrium with their respective mortal communities. The fact that Ahlat employs a priesthood who intercedes with the mortal community on his behalf (and, notably, vice-versa) instead of just taking what he wants is evidence of that. If Ahlat had only acted the part of the insatiable, rapacious predator, <i>there would not be a community there</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-18-2019, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T23:33:47-08:00","id":1289118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289115#post1289115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that the Syndics of Whitewall and Ahlat in Harborhead have reached a sort of equilibrium with their respective mortal communities. The fact that Ahlat employs a priesthood who intercedes with the mortal community on his behalf (and, notably, vice-versa) instead of just taking what he wants is evidence of that. If Ahlat had only acted the part of the insatiable, rapacious predator, <i>there would not be a community there</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there would be. Gods who are powerful and can bribe their way into getting away with it can form a society based on themselves and their whims. The only thing mortals can do is pray or die because the god manipulates the area so they all suffer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T23:40:11-08:00","id":1289119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289112#post1289112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean like harborhead which is much closer to the blessed isle than white wall or a bunch of other places which are screwed because strong gods take over an area? Mortals can get lucky or be incredibly screwed. You can't send someone as strong as Alhat or the syndicates against a mortal army. That's just an easy slaughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are assuming the only recourse for an unruly god (or supernatural threat in general) is to beat their ass like a drum until they cry uncle or die. Most of them aren't that hard to bribe into some sort of workable coexistence deal where you give them things in exchange for leaving you alone or maybe even giving some blessings in return. And if they can't? You can also always try bribing a different one (god, exalted, demon, whatever) of some sort to intercede on your behalf instead.<br /> <br /> And if diplomacy of any kind is just a total no go? Most gods can only dream they were in the power league a regional war god like Ahlat is. Seriously, the vast vast vast majority of them aren't going to come even <i>remotely</i> close. Its not entirely out of reason your local shaman can somehow find their esoteric weakness and you use that to shank them. Or if you are part of the Realm you just tough it out until an immaculate dragon blooded can be dispatched to commence the ass drumming. The Unquiet dead? They have fairly uniform weaknesses (and if they aren't a ghost they can't even turn intangible) on top of generally being pretty low on the supernatural totem pole so its even more likely you can totally take them without needing supernatural intercession on your behalf. The Fae? Really rare even by supernatural standards in most of Creation and the parts they aren't everyone definitely knows they are weak to things like cold iron. Though we aren't sure if they can turn intangible or what their general power level is yet. Lastly the exalted are basically the rarest thing in Creation and if you play your cards right (and especially if they are younger ones not fully come to their power) they are pretty susceptible to getting dog piled and having pointy things shoved into them until they stop being a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-18-2019, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T23:45:32-08:00","id":1289120,"title":"","content":"Oh, right, and demons. Also pretty rare compared to gods and the undead and most of the ones you are likely to run into by those unlikely to appear at all standards are first circles you can probably take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T00:03:54-08:00","id":1289122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289119#post1289119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are assuming the only recourse for an unruly god (or supernatural threat in general) is to beat their ass like a drum until they cry uncle or die. Most of them aren't that hard to bribe into some sort of workable coexistence deal where you give them things in exchange for leaving you alone or maybe even giving some blessings in return. And if they can't? You can also always try bribing a different one (god, exalted, demon, whatever) of some sort to intercede on your behalf instead.<br /> <br /> And if diplomacy of any kind is just a total no go? Most gods can only dream they were in the power league a regional war god like Ahlat is. Seriously, the vast vast vast majority of them aren't going to come even <i>remotely</i> close. Its not entirely out of reason your local shaman can somehow find their esoteric weakness and you use that to shank them. Or if you are part of the Realm you just tough it out until an immaculate dragon blooded can be dispatched to commence the ass drumming. The Unquiet dead? They have fairly uniform weaknesses (and if they aren't a ghost they can't even turn intangible) on top of generally being pretty low on the supernatural totem pole so its even more likely you can totally take them without needing supernatural intercession on your behalf. The Fae? Really rare even by supernatural standards in most of Creation and the parts they aren't everyone definitely knows they are weak to things like cold iron. Though we aren't sure if they can turn intangible or what their general power level is yet. Lastly the exalted are basically the rarest thing in Creation and if you play your cards right (and especially if they are younger ones not fully come to their power) they are pretty susceptible to getting dog piled and having pointy things shoved into them until they stop being a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>The further you go to the edge of the threshold the less of a chance you have. Yes, the threshold means freedom. It also means predation from gods and a host of other things. Even the dragon blooded don't go too far because it does get more wild. In all the editions it's been that way, yes the realm is an imperial empire but at the same time they have wealth, safety and stability. The threshold has freedom but at the cost of safety. There are threats that mortal shaman can't even hope to handle at all. And gods and sorcerers who take advantage of people. Also, there are more than a few celestial gods who use the current state to forcibly build cults to give themselves more power as well as elements and terrestrial gods who no longer care about following rules. Realm Dragon-blooded only have 14k and they're already busy as hell making sure their lands and strapies do their job. Outcastes might help but who knows if they are capable and have immaculate dragon styles to actually deal with spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-18-2019, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T00:21:22-08:00","id":1289125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289122#post1289122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The further you go to the edge of the threshold the less of a chance you have. Yes, the threshold means freedom. It also means predation from gods and a host of other things. Even the dragon blooded don't go too far because it does get more wild. In all the editions it's been that way, yes the realm is an imperial empire but at the same time they have wealth, safety and stability. The threshold has freedom but at the cost of safety. There are threats that mortal shaman can't even hope to handle at all. And gods and sorcerers who take advantage of people. Also, there are more than a few celestial gods who use the current state to forcibly build cults to give themselves more power as well as elements and terrestrial gods who no longer care about following rules. Dragon-blooded only have 10k and they're already busy as hell making sure their lands and strapies do their job. Outcastes might help but who knows if they are capable and have immaculate dragon styles to actually deal with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling you are <i>really</i> overestimating the number of supernatural beings that are<br /> <br /> 1# Completely and totally unreasonable to the point it is utterly impossible to work out some sort of deal with them that leaves the mortal population a decent standard of living<br /> <br /> 2# Too powerful to take out if a large number of mortals motivated to kill them is intent on using occult wisdom from shamans and such to dredge up their weaknesses then dog pile them for being a prick.<br /> <br /> 3# Doesn't have any other local supernatural beings of a more reasonable bent in the area (like a bunch of ghosts pissed some god is screwing with their descendants or a god pissed a nephwrack is killing their worshippers) that can aid the mortals against them in a meaningful way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T00:45:15-08:00","id":1289127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289125#post1289125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get the feeling you are <i>really</i> overestimating the number of supernatural beings that are<br /> <br /> 1# Completely and totally unreasonable to the point it is utterly impossible to work out some sort of deal with them that leaves the mortal population a decent standard of living<br /> <br /> 2# Too powerful to take out if a large number of mortals motivated to kill them is intent on using occult wisdom from shamans and such to dredge up their weaknesses then dog pile them for being a prick.<br /> <br /> 3# Doesn't have any other local supernatural beings of a more reasonable bent in the area (like a bunch of ghosts pissed some god is screwing with their descendants or a god pissed a nephwrack is killing their worshippers) that can aid the mortals against them in a meaningful way.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) has been an issue since the first edition, which was stated and shown in may ways. The gods are just as asholish as demons are if not worse. They get drunk with power and don't give a shit. This is why the Immaculate philosophy exists in the first place and why the sidereals worked hard to force the gods to behave on the blessed isle.<br /> <br /> 2) Is impossible to do without celestial spirit killing charms or Immaculate MA (explicitly the pinnacle of wood dragon). A shaman can beat a spirit but without the charms of the exalted, they'll just come back. This is why exalted were created in the first place. Shaman do not get to have the same amount of power as an exalt. The setting doesn't work that way.<br /> <br /> 2A) Not all exalted have the abilities necessary to fight a god.<br /> <br /> 3) The only thing that really matters is the biggest guy in the room not the most moral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T01:13:53-08:00","id":1289128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) has been an issue since the first edition, which was stated and shown in may ways. The gods are just as asholish as demons are if not worse. They get drunk with power and don't give a shit. This is why the Immaculate philosophy exists in the first place and why the sidereals worked hard to force the gods to behave on the blessed isle. </div> </div> </div>It exists to enforce dragonblooded rule of the world that has the bronze faction manipulating it from the shadows. As we saw from chapter fiction in WFHW the 'offenses' monks are sent out to quash tend to be things like 'granting fertility blessings in exchange for extra worship instead of settling for the Immaculate tithe' instead of things like 'ordering villages to sacrifice every child born in the first week of a month'. Some gods may be jerks but they are jerks that can only get worship from <i>living</i> mortals and have a lot of divine (or other kind of supernatural) competition that would be happy to steal their cult and (in some cases) happy to engineer their fall to assume their portfolio.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Is impossible to do without celestial spirit killing charms or Immaculate MA (explicitly the pinnacle of wood dragon). A shaman can beat a spirit but without the charms of the exalted, they'll just come back. This is why exalted were created in the first place. Shaman do not get to have the same amount of power as an exalt. The setting doesn't work that way.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Completely wrong, go reread the antagonist chapter in the core on spirits. First circle demons and elementals anyone can kill in one go, Ghosts have to have a strong will to survive their second death (let alone a 3rd, 4th, and etc), and gods can be killed permanently by destroying their sanctum/respawn point or chain killing them until they are too weakened to reform (each death weakens them) and asshole gods who pissed off their base so hard they rose up and ganked them aren't likely to have the cult rating needed to hang in there in the face of those. Also, a god so humbled by being killed once in the prime of their power is probably going to think twice about starting shit again while they are weakened. Those charms are a short cut not the only way to do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) The only thing that really matters is the biggest guy in the room not the most moral. </div> </div> </div>Then one day the big guy in the room dies because it turned out they had been spiking his food with arsenic instead of challenging him to a boxing match.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-18-2019, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T01:34:18-08:00","id":1289130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289128#post1289128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It exists to enforce dragonblooded rule of the world that has the bronze faction manipulating it from the shadows. As we saw from chapter fiction in WFHW the 'offenses' monks are sent out to quash tend to be things like 'granting fertility blessings in exchange for extra worship instead of settling for the Immaculate tithe' instead of things like 'ordering villages to sacrifice every child born in the first week of a month'. Some gods may be jerks but they are jerks that can only get worship from <i>living</i> mortals and have a lot of divine (or other kind of supernatural) competition that would be happy to steal their cult and (in some cases) happy to engineer their fall to assume their portfolio.</div> </div> </div> </div> That isn't the only reason dragon-blooded do it and if you actually read the supporting 1e fiction and situations that 3e builds off of it you'd know that gods don't give a fuck and the strong ones are almost unassailable without exalted enforcing the peace. Gods are full on assholes. Most of them don't care about humans except as a prayer battery and have no problem sucking the resources for themselves. The immaculate philosophy is such mixed force because it's a lie but one that benefits humans from the predation of gods. It starts with a blessing for extra worship and slowly grows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Completely wrong, go reread the antagonist chapter in the core on spirits. First circle demons and elementals anyone can kill in one go, Ghosts have to have a strong will to survive their second death (let alone a 3rd, 4th, and etc), and gods can be killed permanently by destroying their sanctum/respawn point or chain killing them until they are too weakened to reform (each death weakens them) and asshole gods who pissed off their base so hard they rose up and ganked them aren't likely to have the cult rating needed to hang in there in the face of those. Also, a god so humbled by being killed once in the prime of their power is probably going to think twice about starting shit again while they are weakened. Those charms are a short cut not the only way to do it. </div> </div> </div> These won't be possible if the thing in question is E4 or above for mortals. There's no way for them to be strong enough to take him on shaman or no and the death of a weaker god will only be a set back for a while before it comes back. That's not to mention the charms that manipulate the environment to spite the mortals for attacking him. This also doesn't account for the mortals or lesser spirits who will still protect the god because they fear the consequences.<br /> <br /> Honestly, you over estimate what mortals can do even in a block. They can probably deal with minor spirits but the moment anything with any power comes they have no chance without the exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then one day the big guy in the room dies because it turned out they had been spiking his food with arsenic instead of challenging him to a boxing match. </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't matter because he's a god and immune to arsenic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-18-2019, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T04:27:23-08:00","id":1289143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289130#post1289130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which doesn't matter because he's a god and immune to arsenic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you cite that, please? Last I checked, Ahlat has fourteen dice to resist poison, which is pretty beefy, but it's a far shot from immunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-18-2019, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T05:09:12-08:00","id":1289148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That isn't the only reason dragon-blooded do it and if you actually read the supporting 1e fiction and situations that 3e builds off of it you'd know that gods don't give a fuck and the strong ones are almost unassailable without exalted enforcing the peace. Gods are full on assholes. Most of them don't care about humans except as a prayer battery and have no problem sucking the resources for themselves. The immaculate philosophy is such mixed force because it's a lie but one that benefits humans from the predation of gods. It starts with a blessing for extra worship and slowly grows. </div> </div> </div>They would go after the really bad ones regardless of its existence, the purpose of the order is to cement dragon blooded rule among the spirits and that just happens to include smacking around the really bad ones as well as icing on the cake of their intent as a weapon to keep gods in line with their 'proper' place receiving their allotted portion of the prayer and doing nothing outside their job description like give fertility blessings and such (unless thats actually your heavenly mandated job, of course).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These won't be possible if the thing in question is E4 or above for mortals. There's no way for them to be strong enough to take him on shaman or no and the death of a weaker god will only be a set back for a while before it comes back. That's not to mention the charms that manipulate the environment to spite the mortals for attacking him. This also doesn't account for the mortals or lesser spirits who will still protect the god because they fear the consequences.<br /> <br /> Honestly, you over estimate what mortals can do even in a block. They can probably deal with minor spirits but the moment anything with any power comes they have no chance without the exalted. </div> </div> </div>And here we go back to what I'm saying from the start, you vastly overestimate how many of those there are. Most spirits we have seen written up were in the essence 1-3 (EX: Storm mothers are only 3) range, thats the standard. The beings higher then that tended to be incredibly high up the ladder beings like a directional god of war (Ahlat). You would have to be <i>incredibly</i> unlucky if the spirit being harassing you ended up being something that is essence 4+<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which doesn't matter because he's a god and immune to arsenic. </div> </div> </div>Feel free to replace arsenic with some other underhanded strategy that involves coming at him from the side instead of playing their game and challenging them to a straight up slugfest like they specialize in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T06:05:33-08:00","id":1289160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289118#post1289118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, there would be. Gods who are powerful and can bribe their way into getting away with it can form a society based on themselves and their whims. The only thing mortals can do is pray or die because the god manipulates the area so they all suffer.</div> </div> </div> </div>This explains a lot, and also displays a perspective on the setting that is so incompatible that I can't really think of an effective avenue for counterargument.<br /> <br /> I will say one thing, though:<br /> <br /> Considering how this conversation is being driven by your frustration with seeming contradictions in and shortcomings of the setting, it might be worth considering that a lot of those issues are arising from some base assumptions about how the setting (and general relationships and power dynamics) works that aren't shared by the people writing it, and the reason they don't have those assumptions is not because they're dumb and wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T07:43:39-08:00","id":1289185,"title":"","content":"Just as a point of matter, We the Shogunate would like to remind you that Dragonbloods controlled all of Creation at one time, out to the edges, and it was bigger back then too. And we did this despite spending most of our time fighting wars against each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T09:47:41-08:00","id":1289213,"title":"","content":"So, Eric in his interview mentioned a number of dominions, and one he said wasn't really focused on the Realm at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:04:01-08:00","id":1289223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289037#post1289037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This really interests me. Why is this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Appreciated that you'd ask (not everyone would ask about things going against their argument). I'm in two minds about responding as I don't really have a very good response as an argument though - more of a gut feeling that it wouldn't be very complementary to playing up the characters individual motivating forces, rather more distracting or distorting.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> On the recent thread drift, I have to admit that, it being not credible so that mortals could threaten the Realm and seriously degrade it without Lunars and hence Lunars needed to struggle against the Realm (an earlier comment in thread), but mortals simultaneously being well able to resist gods without the Realm is a bit the opposite than I would have thought. (If this is at all a fair summary). After all, per the original 1e rationale for the Immaculates, gods are the ones the Dragonblooded specifically came up with (or rather the Sidereals came up) with Celestial Martial Arts styles beyond their normal limits and capacities and those of mortals to fight, once Celestials were less available to them and the duties fell to the Dragonblooded (rather than the Celestials as the intercessors in the hierarchy of the First Age).<br /> <br /> That is, if anything, Dragonblooded are human bodied men and women who mortals can do something against, while spirits are sort of difficult for mortals to get any purchase. Mortals greater relative advantage vs DB, while DB relative advantage greater vs spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T10:40:12-08:00","id":1289229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289223#post1289223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit that, it being not credible so that mortals could threaten the Realm and seriously degrade it without Lunars and hence Lunars needed to struggle against the Realm (an earlier comment in thread), but mortals simultaneously being well able to resist gods without the Realm is a bit the opposite than I would have thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Militarily, there are numerous examples of a for that is stronger on paper ultimately losing or withdrawing because the conditions for victory are sufficiently frustrating or inconveniencing that they'd prefer to make a settlement, or give up entirely.<br /> <br /> The United States is making peace overtures to the Taliban. The Taliban didn't suddenly develop their own drones.<br /> <br /> Socially and economically, negotiation from a position of weakness is a thing. It's a thing based on accepting that you're constrained to give up something, but through clever presentation, a bit of cunning, maybe harnessing conflicts or divisions in the other side, and appeals to their better nature (or at least their vanity), it's possible to give up more manageable quantities. That's when the stronger party doesn't enter with an intent to be more reasonable.<br /> <br /> These systems are only binary if one believes solely in zero-sum games, which is ludicrous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, per the original 1e rationale for the Immaculates, gods are the ones the Dragonblooded specifically came up with (or rather the Sidereals came up) with Celestial Martial Arts styles beyond their normal limits and capacities and those of mortals to fight, once Celestials were less available to them and the duties fell to the Dragonblooded (rather than the Celestials as the intercessors in the hierarchy of the First Age).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Immaculate narrative about the nature of gods is not completely inaccurate, but it's still a bad idea to take the justifications of an authoritarian society at face value. Not all gods require the constant threat of force to not continuously exploit mortals, not least because sometimes the threat only needs to be made once and it sticks. Some cultures would prefer the authority of their traditional gods to that of the Realm, and not even just because it's lighter; people can be averse to an alien and intrusive culture as a matter of principle.<br /> <br /> And for all the Immaculate posturing, the Realm still negotiates with many gods. Salt gods may have constraints in negotiation, but at the end of the day they're still getting a percentage of the value of an important commodity. After enough generations, it would be a bad idea for Immaculates to enforce their compliance through brute force even if they were able; too much of Realm finances is valued based on the rate of taxes for the sacrifices to the salt gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T11:09:33-08:00","id":1289237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289128#post1289128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It exists to enforce dragonblooded rule of the world that has the bronze faction manipulating it from the shadows. As we saw from chapter fiction in WFHW the 'offenses' monks are sent out to quash tend to be things like 'granting fertility blessings in exchange for extra worship instead of settling for the Immaculate tithe' instead of things like 'ordering villages to sacrifice every child born in the first week of a month'. Some gods may be jerks but they are jerks that can only get worship from <i>living</i> mortals and have a lot of divine (or other kind of supernatural) competition that would be happy to steal their cult and (in some cases) happy to engineer their fall to assume their portfolio.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the immaculate faith is largely a tool of social and political control, tying the ruling class of the world (the dragonblooded) to a state of spiritual perfection and enforcing a belief that servitude to them is the natural state of the world, it does also have clear and important benefits for the people of Creation. There is no mythical Free Market for worship, if you tell the local disease god that you'll vote with your prayer elsewhere, you will suffer for it until you regret it and have to worship from an even worse position than before. If you tell the local village god to get lost because it demands a sacrifice, it doesnt get replaced by a nicer god with better rates, it tells everyone else that YOU are the sacrifice this time and they will comply to not be horrifically murdered by something powerful and immortal. The world of Creation is a miserable place for mortals to live in. The gods are capricious, cruel and selfish, they have grown intensely corrupt and the sidereals are far too stretched to ever deal with even a fraction of their abuses. Monks of the immaculate faith are a genuine force for good in many parts of the world, as they are the only thing standing between oppressed peasants and the spirits preying on them. Broadly speaking this is not altruistic as the Immaculate Faith spreading is part of how the Realm maintains its political power in the world, and getting rid of tyrannical gods is also removing rival powers to their own control over the threshold, but it's hard to get upset about this when a monk just threw the local farm spirit off a cliff for threatening to starve you unless you pray 14 hours a day to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T11:24:25-08:00","id":1289242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289185#post1289185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as a point of matter, We the Shogunate would like to remind you that Dragonbloods controlled all of Creation at one time, out to the edges, and it was bigger back then too. And we did this despite spending most of our time fighting wars against each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>You also have to remember this was before the contagion when they were at millions of dragon blooded. The numbers were literally around 100x what the are now.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T11:32:57-08:00","id":1289245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289160#post1289160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This explains a lot, and also displays a perspective on the setting that is so incompatible that I can't really think of an effective avenue for counterargument.<br /> <br /> I will say one thing, though:<br /> <br /> Considering how this conversation is being driven by your frustration with seeming contradictions in and shortcomings of the setting, it might be worth considering that a lot of those issues are arising from some base assumptions about how the setting (and general relationships and power dynamics) works that aren't shared by the people writing it, and the reason they don't have those assumptions is not because they're dumb and wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way? I've read the books up and down from 1e on and the gods are dicks. Some of them aren't too bad but others just don't care and will do anything to improve. Unless the new writers are changing the nature of the gods, I can assume it's still the same. The thread drift though was from how the threshold just isn't controllable with the numbers the dragon blooded have, even without the lunars. Who are a formidable but also just one of many threats that keep the threshold what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T13:45:42-08:00","id":1289297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289245#post1289245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In what way? I've read the books up and down from 1e on and the gods are dicks. Some of them aren't too bad but others just don't care and will do anything to improve. Unless the new writers are changing the nature of the gods, I can assume it's still the same. The thread drift though was from how the threshold just isn't controllable with the numbers the dragon blooded have, even without the lunars. Who are a formidable but also just one of many threats that keep the threshold what it is. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I can't speak for other writers (and certainly not the devs), but &quot;Gods are full-on assholes, but a few are okay&quot; is not an assumption I write from. I write from the assumption that gods are venal and self-centered by human standards, because their nature gives them little capacity to relate to many human struggles. They tend toward shocking short-sightedness and mind-boggling far-sightedness, which may make them seem more </span></span></span><i>callous</i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">,</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">but on average they aren't innately more or less </span></span></span><i>cruel or violent</i> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">than humans are. Even gods out in the middle of nowhere (by human standards) have relationships, want ways to make their jobs/lives easier or more rewarding, and can respond to other overtures with generosity or hostility, as they feel is warranted. Even corrupt gods of a fallen age have some incentive to think cooperatively because, to borrow a popular phrase, they live in a society. The horror of gods in Exalted is not that they are hateful or unrelatable, but that their motivations are banal and relatable. Their natures make them no more or less monstrous than any powerful person who's had the privilege not to experience certain hardships, or who thought that their problems were more important than anyone else's.<br /> <br /> Put another way, a god is the sort of person that might hear you talk about having lost your entire family to a wasting plague, and respond that their favorite tree died thirty years ago, because they think those losses are similar in scope. Depending on their attitude, that might lead them to try to empathize, or to tell you to shrug it off, and they might become gravely offended if you object either way. Conversely, if you show appreciation for their condescending wisdom, they might favor you with a blessing or even their personal attention.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289223#post1289223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Appreciated that you'd ask (not everyone would ask about things going against their argument). I'm in two minds about responding as I don't really have a very good response as an argument though - more of a gut feeling that it wouldn't be very complementary to playing up the characters individual motivating forces, rather more distracting or distorting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to be able to interrogate our own processes.<br /> <br /> Give it some thought. If you come up with anything else, hit me up on Twitter. I'm easy enough to find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 02-18-2019, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T14:41:24-08:00","id":1289316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289297#post1289297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I can't speak for other writers (and certainly not the devs), but &quot;Gods are full-on assholes, but a few are okay&quot; is not an assumption I write from. I write from the assumption that gods are venal and self-centered by human standards, because their nature gives them little capacity to relate to many human struggles. They tend toward shocking short-sightedness and mind-boggling far-sightedness, which may make them seem more </span></span></span><i>callous</i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">,</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">but on average they aren't innately more or less </span></span></span><i>cruel or violent</i> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">than humans are. Even gods out in the middle of nowhere (by human standards) have relationships, want ways to make their jobs/lives easier or more rewarding, and can respond to other overtures with generosity or hostility, as they feel is warranted. Even corrupt gods of a fallen age have some incentive to think cooperatively because, to borrow a popular phrase, they live in a society. The horror of gods in Exalted is not that they are hateful or unrelatable, but that their motivations are banal and relatable. Their natures make them no more or less monstrous than any powerful person who's had the privilege not to experience certain hardships, or who thought that their problems were more important than anyone else's.<br /> <br /> Put another way, a god is the sort of person that might hear you talk about having lost your entire family to a wasting plague, and respond that their favorite tree died thirty years ago, because they think those losses are similar in scope. Depending on their attitude, that might lead them to try to empathize, or to tell you to shrug it off, and they might become gravely offended if you object either way. Conversely, if you show appreciation for their condescending wisdom, they might favor you with a blessing or even their personal attention.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> </div>That is on the whole is quite different from 1e where gods in the fallen age have blatantly extorted prayer and when egregious enough made slaves of populations all for the sake of their own whims. One of more interesting things about gods is how petty and human like they really are and how easily they'll abuse them to get more power. It was also these tenets which forced the immaculate order to be a peacekeeping force which makes it much more nuanced then what people in this thread might believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T15:05:00-08:00","id":1289322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289316#post1289316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is on the whole is quite different from 1e where gods in the fallen age have blatantly extorted prayer and when egregious enough made slaves of populations all for the sake of their own whims.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quite certain that gods in this Edition have done that as well.<br /> <br /> Not all of them.<br /> <br /> Same as in First Edition.<br /> <br /> Non-zero sum game!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of more interesting things about gods is how petty and human like they really are and how easily they'll abuse them to get more power.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're human like, but have no variation and are all exploitative and terrible?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">makes it much more nuanced then what people in this thread might believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think everybody else's view is unnuanced?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T15:09:50-08:00","id":1289326,"title":"","content":"You know there\u2019s a lot of space between \u201cThe Realm would control all of Creation were it not for Lunars\u201d and \u201cThe Realm would be the exact same size as it is now even without Lunars,\u201d right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T15:17:55-08:00","id":1289328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289322#post1289322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm quite certain that gods in this Edition have done that as well.<br /> <br /> Not all of them.<br /> <br /> Same as in First Edition.<br /> <br /> Non-zero sum game!</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that not all of them do that but most of them do. If they didn't the celestial bureaucracy and and the terrestrial courts would be in a much better state than they are. However, rather than fix the issues plaguing Yu Shan and creation they instead took advantage of the situation and continue to profit from it. It wasn't just the bronze allied gods who did this but also the threshold gods and the terrestrial ones who don't care about anything more than expansion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're human like, but have no variation and are all exploitative and terrible? </div> </div> </div>I guess to be topical. I see most of them as CEOs. Some of them are pretty good people and I'm sure most of them are affable but that doesn't stop them from doing horrible things in the name of profits. I'm also sure that some of them for example that field god started out with good intentions but the extortion of prayer will only lead to bigger issues down the line. It'll start to demand more as it's given more, unsatisfied it will begin to do more down the line to solidify more power and grow past his own purview.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You think everybody else's view is unnuanced? </div> </div> </div>I guess that comment was more about the IO. The IO started as a mixed bag it shouldn't be as black and white as Mizu has been stating it is. Yes, it was created for the promotion of dragon-blooded hegemony but the order has also done a lot of good things. To say that ALL gods are one way or another would be wrong. However, the older editions stressed that MOST of the gods were corrupt and because most of them were corrupt not much could be done about it. Because if enough of them tried they could have fixed the issue by now. Which is part of the tragedy of the current state of things, the world is broken on all levels. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T15:39:38-08:00","id":1289332,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... There's a lot written about the gods in Exalted for us to draw on.<br /> <br /> I think there are certainly Gods of Pegana-esque uncaring, selfish cruel sorts among them. And I think this is intentional. So I have sympathy with Epimetheus's comment there.<br /> <br /> And there's the intent that Geoff Grabowski was quite interested in the idea of portraying transactions between gods and humans with the potential for abuse, unregulated by any higher authority that bound them to a code of law and behaviour (with some degree of skepticism towards this probably from his unique pol.sci background?). I'm thinking of his comments about Ahlat and his tassels here.<br /> <br /> But you always have Fakharu and Vanileth and the Golden Lord and suchlike about, who are fairly admirable in their own way.<br /> <br /> More usually I think the gods are akin to the river god portrayed in the Exalted 2e intro fic, in which they are somewhat blind to the consequences of their actions on the material world and the minds and feelings of mortals and tend to be caught up in large passions and obsessions and status projects.<br /> <br /> In general, I think the sentiment would make sense that the gods are generally necessary and somewhat admirable, but the relationship of man and Heaven benefits from the regulation and intercession of the Exalted to create harmony. Which is not to say that this intercession must take violent forms, though the Exalted probably need to back at least the potential for that - it can be the persuasion through the supernaturally skilled and infused words and deeds and dealmaking of the Exalted, as much or more than violence. You're here to restore the proper relationship of heaven and earth, fundamentally, and seems fundamentally one in which you are a conciliator. (Assuming you're not one of Rakan Thulio's anti-heaven hit squad, I guess!).<br /> <br /> This is probably even more important for 3e, because Exigency seems to me to benefit from gods being somewhat admirable patrons who have limits on their ability to interact healthily with humanity directly (though Exigency seems decreasingly emphasized as a 3e thing as the edition rolls on, and I feel this won't cut much ice with Epimetheus as, if I recall correctly, he's not into it).<br /> <br /> (This may also be a particularly touchy subject that I suspect the Exalted community has probably handled badly, and to get further onto a tangent - if it were possible - probably because the meta-conversation around the Yozis was of a sort of &quot;If you hurt humans and you don't get it without being told why through supernatural diplomacy why its bad, you're still evil and we don't owe you anything. But anyway, the Yozis were totally malicious in the time before the First Age. So.&quot;. But that's another tangent for another day.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T20:06:39-08:00","id":1289391,"title":"","content":"I might think of gods and worshippers a lot like the relationship between Medieval aristocrats and their villeins.<br /> <br /> A subject that is often viewed in narratives widely distorted by the lenses of things such as Whig history, Victorian self-satisfaction, and the writings of Karl Marx.<br /> <br /> But, from more credible historical sources I've read on it, it basically forms the basis for everything I was saying before about people adapting to minimize the impact of a small-scale oppressive system on them.<br /> <br /> For instance, an idea that the worshippers of a god that is taking too many liberties might send people out to seek the aid of Immaculate monks, or other less systemic forms of redress.<br /> <br /> You're not getting many gods above Essence 4. Their capacity to restrain sufficiently determined people can be limited. There are a lot of conceivable situations where the god will back down.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Philosophy might have an impact in places that the least of monks has never so much as heard of, simply by reputation.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that there's a lot about this scenario that would be modelled with the social system. How good is your local god's Resolve? Do they have any strong Principles that will bolster them against such threats? Any social magic to reinforce their own personality?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289332#post1289332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(This may also be a particularly touchy subject that I suspect the Exalted community has probably handled badly, and to get further onto a tangent - if it were possible - probably because the meta-conversation around the Yozis was of a sort of &amp;quot;If you hurt humans and you don't get it without being told why through supernatural diplomacy why its bad, you're still evil and we don't owe you anything. But anyway, the Yozis were totally malicious in the time before the First Age. So.&amp;quot;. But that's another tangent for another day.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohoho, I've had some thoughts ready and waiting for this subject for weeks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T20:26:54-08:00","id":1289397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is probably even more important for 3e, because Exigency seems to me to benefit from gods being somewhat admirable patrons who have limits on their ability to interact healthily with humanity directly (though Exigency seems decreasingly emphasized as a 3e thing as the edition rolls on, and I feel this won't cut much ice with Epimetheus as, if I recall correctly, he's not into it). </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't see it as them getting less emphasis. It makes sense to get the classic 5 out first then do the books for the new ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T20:28:30-08:00","id":1289398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289316#post1289316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is on the whole is quite different from 1e where gods in the fallen age have blatantly extorted prayer and when egregious enough made slaves of populations all for the sake of their own whims. One of more interesting things about gods is how petty and human like they really are and how easily they'll abuse them to get more power. It was also these tenets which forced the immaculate order to be a peacekeeping force which makes it much more nuanced then what people in this thread might believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really on a whole different level because, as you just pointed out, gods are petty and human in many ways, and humans have and do blatantly extort resources and make slaves of entire populations for the sake of their own whims. Many gods are monstrous because many humans, when given power and privilege, or when made desperate by deprivation, are monstrous. But gods live in too social a milieu for them mostly treat the world as--as Isator said--a zero-sum game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T00:25:10-08:00","id":1289440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289397#post1289397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I don't see it as them getting less emphasis. It makes sense to get the classic 5 out first then do the books for the new ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not going like that; next fatsplat after Fangs is Exigents, and Getimians are planned to come out in close proximity to Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T01:15:00-08:00","id":1289446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289440#post1289440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're not going like that; next fatsplat after Fangs is Exigents, and Getimians are planned to come out in close proximity to Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Huh, for some reason I thought after Lunars it was going to be Abyssal&gt;Sidereal&gt;Exigent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T01:26:47-08:00","id":1289448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289446#post1289446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Huh, for some reason I thought after Lunars it was going to be Abyssal&gt;Sidereal&gt;Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>You must have been assuming based on previous editions. Last we heard, the plan (which is subject to change, hence Lunars and Exigents having swapped places from earlier in line) was....<br /> <br /> Lunars<br /> Exigents (with the Umbral Exalted, Dream-Souled, and Heart-Eaters in its appendix)<br /> Sidereals (Getimians as a paperback length supplement shortly after)<br /> Abyssals (Liminals as a paperback length supplement shortly after)<br /> <br /> Most likely followed by Infernals and then Alchemicals, one would assume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T02:18:39-08:00","id":1289450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289448#post1289448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You must have been assuming based on previous editions. Last we heard, the plan (which is subject to change, hence Lunars and Exigents having swapped places from earlier in line) was....<br /> <br /> Lunars<br /> Exigents (with the Umbral Exalted, Dream-Souled, and Heart-Eaters in its appendix)<br /> Sidereals (Getimians as a paperback length supplement shortly after)<br /> Abyssals (Liminals as a paperback length supplement shortly after)<br /> <br /> Most likely followed by Infernals and then Alchemicals, one would assume.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK, the last Vance said, all of the splatbooks were going to be hardbacks, Getimians and Liminals being shorter than the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T02:41:44-08:00","id":1289451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289448#post1289448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You must have been assuming based on previous editions. Last we heard, the plan (which is subject to change, hence Lunars and Exigents having swapped places from earlier in line) was....<br /> <br /> Lunars<br /> Exigents (with the Umbral Exalted, Dream-Souled, and Heart-Eaters in its appendix)<br /> Sidereals (Getimians as a paperback length supplement shortly after)<br /> Abyssals (Liminals as a paperback length supplement shortly after)<br /> <br /> Most likely followed by Infernals and then Alchemicals, one would assume.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh, if the Abyssal splat book is really that far off I hope they decide to just release necromancy in a supplement instead of making us wait what will probably be 3 years when thats supposed to be a power for all exalts to use like evocations, sorcery, and martial arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T22:54:26-08:00","id":1289820,"title":"","content":"Looking at their Great Curse, I wonder how many Lunars felt unconcerned about the Realm, until its policies and power projection was ultimately responsible for creating constraints and frustrations that provoked an especially nasty Monstrous Urge, and the Lunar projects the blame for that event onto the Realm.<br /> <br /> Conversely, I wonder how many Lunars have a bad experience of extreme reactions to infringement upon their freedom (or general frustration with something not going their way), and thus respond by trying to exert themselves over their surroundings and order things as they will to remove those irritations, thus themselves repealing the freedoms of others.<br /> <br /> There are things in the Lunar Essence that guide them in the direction of safeguarding, preserving, promoting systems bigger than themselves, but the Curse can gnaw at them, making such systems and associations feel nothing but static and stifling, telling you that you know best and the ignorant, hidebound creatures who will never know a multitude of forms and ways of being are unworthy of disregarding you, and sometimes when you try to ignore it too much a little bit of your humanity slips out of place and the Curse tells you to spend just a little while indulging in what <i>real</i> freedom is (when of course the obsessive pursuits in an uninhibited state are even more constraining than people that won't listen to you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T00:00:54-08:00","id":1289836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289450#post1289450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> AFAIK, the last Vance said, all of the splatbooks were going to be hardbacks, Getimians and Liminals being shorter than the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Update: asked on the &quot;Ask the Devs&quot; thread, and Eric said that currently they're thinking of doing Getimians and Liminals as softbacks, although that's still subject to change.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T01:48:31-08:00","id":1289849,"title":"","content":"I suspect how receptive people are to the charm design guidelines in Exigents is going to be a major indicator of if that's practical or not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T06:56:23-08:00","id":1291521,"title":"","content":"Getting back to the original topic, I don't think that Lunars is too focused on the Realm given all of the lore and fiction we've seen so far of Lunars clowning Solars, Abyssals, Infernals, Sidereals, other Lunars, Liminals, Exigents, gods, demons, ghosts, and mortals like they clown the Realm.<br /> <br /> *Checks notes*<br /> <br /> Oh wait, the opposite of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T07:19:30-08:00","id":1291526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OjsTloR1NLo\" data-code=\"OjsTloR1NLo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/OjsTloR1NLo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T13:05:00-08:00","id":1291584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1289213#post1289213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Eric in his interview mentioned a number of dominions, and one he said wasn't really focused on the Realm at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>To elaborate, one of the dominions written up in Chapter 3 is completely unconcerned with the Realm (they're focused on rival mortal societies and on the Fair Folk), while three or four others have spent generations or centuries being more or less unconcerned with the Realm and are only focusing on it now that the Empress is gone and a Realm civil war looms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T13:45:26-08:00","id":1291595,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, interesting. Looking forward to reading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T16:26:11-08:00","id":1291651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288173-\u200bare-lunar\u2019s-too-mono-focused-on-the-realm?p=1291584#post1291584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To elaborate, one of the dominions written up in Chapter 3 is completely unconcerned with the Realm (they're focused on rival mortal societies and on the Fair Folk), while three or four others have spent generations or centuries being more or less unconcerned with the Realm and are only focusing on it now that the Empress is gone and a Realm civil war looms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to hear it Mr. Minton, thank you for stopping in. I am really looking forward to reading about dominions!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}